<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="Nothing X App">
  <data key="d0">Nothing X App</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Nothing X App is a software application developed by Nothing Technologies, designed to manage and configure the features of various Nothing earbuds, including the Ear (open), CMF Buds 2, and Neckband Pro models. It serves as a companion application for these devices, allowing users to customize touch gestures, adjust volume, and manage noise cancellation modes. The app provides access to advanced settings such as Dual Connection, Smart ANC, and LDAC audio configuration, enabling users to fine-tune sound quality and device connectivity. It also includes options for customizing EQ settings, sound profiles, and preset sound effects. Additionally, the Nothing X App is used to update firmware, reset settings, and manage Bluetooth connections for the earbuds, ensuring optimal performance and compatibility with both iOS and Android devices. As a recommended troubleshooting tool, it plays a key role in maintaining and enhancing the functionality of Nothing's earbud products.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762fda66ccc0b9dd4cae96c4b09a2422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbad053247bfe41ce192c651034259c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbdc3aa884ec77acb84402d00879691d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1887c3e753e5f27cc1105a32465893f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7729ae6048c026d1b7b5e466d0f1c36c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efdc5389f3967066ca146a24ea33b83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dbcfd0ba7e5f79063be82c76153444e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca8764057d5d820c4c3fb502a440d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39d4901014b867cda8bfaf59458315b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-716596cbb2a7e8b3702d6ceb7f52724e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebeef135007ca56eca4d845a2c04e9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Nothing Ear">
  <data key="d0">Nothing Ear</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Nothing Ear is a product line of wireless earbuds developed by Nothing Technologies, designed to connect with the Nothing Phone and enhance the user experience during calls and gaming. These earbuds are capable of high-definition audio playback via the LDAC codec and include features such as gesture controls for media and call functions. They are marketed as a brand of earphones produced by Nothing, a consumer electronics company, and are mentioned in the context of Bluetooth settings and app connectivity. The product line consists of earbuds and related accessories, offering Bluetooth connectivity, environmental noise cancellation, and compatibility with various devices and operating systems. They utilize the Fast Pair feature for seamless setup with the Nothing Phone and can be managed through the phone’s settings. Additionally, the Nothing Ear is noted for its Dual Connection capability, Bass Enhance feature, and includes a charging case with specific battery capacities and performance metrics. While some descriptions mention potential Bluetooth connection issues during calls, the overall design and functionality of Nothing Ear emphasize a cohesive and integrated audio experience for users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9fb365d0322c82fb6ff52dc4a7925f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762fda66ccc0b9dd4cae96c4b09a2422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-124df9689f92596c4fbc5e0e680893f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d629090523155bf0dd12f9021e8a28a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c10ba86f3c652add8c1d23db1a9625b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d82ee9e80b9a4011cc5dfdad909fc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b8eb92f55e1f3c041c691be7b6dbda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="iOS Device">
  <data key="d0">iOS Device</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">iOS Device is a general term referring to Apple's mobile operating system and devices running it, such as iPhones, which have specific Bluetooth protocol handling and app management settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-762fda66ccc0b9dd4cae96c4b09a2422</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Android Device">
  <data key="d0">Android Device</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">Android Device refers to mobile devices running Google's Android operating system, which have different settings and behaviors for managing background apps and Bluetooth connectivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-762fda66ccc0b9dd4cae96c4b09a2422</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="CMF Watch App">
  <data key="d0">CMF Watch App</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">CMF Watch App is a software application used for managing and pairing Watch Pro devices with phones.&lt;SEP&gt;The CMF Watch App is a software application, possibly related to the Nothing X App, used for connecting to a watch device and experiencing similar disconnection issues due to background app management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-762fda66ccc0b9dd4cae96c4b09a2422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efdc5389f3967066ca146a24ea33b83a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Bluetooth">
  <data key="d0">Bluetooth</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Bluetooth is a wireless communication technology and protocol used for connecting devices over short distances, enabling data transfer and communication between compatible devices. It is widely utilized by various devices such as the Watch Pro, CMF earbuds, Ear (2), Ear (stick), Ear (1), and earbuds in general, to establish connections with mobile devices, phones, and other electronics. This technology facilitates a range of features including audio streaming, music control, phone calls, remote camera control, heart rate monitoring, and volume synchronization. Bluetooth is integral to the operation of devices like the Nothing Phone (1) and the Nothing X App, where it enables pairing and integration with earbuds. However, it can also experience compatibility issues, connection problems, or timeout states, which may affect sound output and connection speed. Additionally, Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) is a specific version of the protocol used by the Watch Pro and Ear (1) earbuds to connect with mobile devices and support features such as phone ringing and app functionality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-762fda66ccc0b9dd4cae96c4b09a2422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01cde718609da4920ebfa164616b8d87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efdc5389f3967066ca146a24ea33b83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca8764057d5d820c4c3fb502a440d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6dc70b538423eed2a153e23decae4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31736155d9fcbf91049d0a9e73805dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ea28975423f6227a8330d76c202878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c923c17927fa4e291cc287467061e0cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e7514c9c486c31232321ac43b9689ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fec2c3e80ab69404ff0b23b014c07483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1937bef2f48d7dfa41b98235ae13df22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d88ccae3cdc762688c1e8d90c4e68c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dbcfd0ba7e5f79063be82c76153444e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39d4901014b867cda8bfaf59458315b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56220d4c1145af0000fc9cb728dc6db7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-136bde614c09969c0d7fb82cc253fd47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7729ae6048c026d1b7b5e466d0f1c36c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a93494f099711f42904d9b1378c73449&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-716596cbb2a7e8b3702d6ceb7f52724e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea57d11556bf408a29dc7c7e37398cc2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="BLE (Bluetooth Low Energy)">
  <data key="d0">BLE (Bluetooth Low Energy)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">BLE is a Bluetooth protocol optimized for low power consumption, used by the Nothing X App to connect to earbuds, which is paused during active calls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-762fda66ccc0b9dd4cae96c4b09a2422</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Background Running Permissions">
  <data key="d0">Background Running Permissions</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Background Running Permissions are settings on a phone that allow an app to run in the background and maintain a connection to a smartwatch.&lt;SEP&gt;Background Running Permissions are settings that determine whether an app can run in the background, affecting Bluetooth and other functionalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-762fda66ccc0b9dd4cae96c4b09a2422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a93494f099711f42904d9b1378c73449</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="App Cache">
  <data key="d0">App Cache</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">App Cache refers to temporary data stored by an app that can cause performance issues if not cleared, and it is a troubleshooting step for the Nothing X App and others.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-762fda66ccc0b9dd4cae96c4b09a2422</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Nothing">
  <data key="d0">Nothing</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Nothing is a technology company that produces a range of consumer electronics, including smartphones and audio devices. It is known for developing products such as the Nothing Phone, which features innovative technologies like the Glyph Interface and Nothing OS, emphasizing sleek design and advanced functionality. The company also manufactures audio devices such as the Buds Pro earbuds and the Neckband Pro, providing support and guidance for their usage and features. Additionally, Nothing develops and supports the Nothing X app, which allows users to customize and manage product features across its devices. It offers technical specifications and testing for its audio products, including battery life, charging protocols, and compatibility. The brand name "Nothing" is used for its mobile phones, and the company provides customer service and technical support for all its devices, including the Watch Pro. Overall, Nothing is a multifaceted organization that focuses on creating innovative and user-friendly technology products in the realm of smartphones and audio devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-762fda66ccc0b9dd4cae96c4b09a2422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36249177cb5d5f7c720a6f64a0edc813&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8464f2a22c355940190a72202a4bd5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbeb4732200e7559b14badeb7c65f47c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb83fc961a06d6a2e205ffa27cd9700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cd614c63bd30923f007ff94a3e7a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9ff89b42c8123f60ebe4521bfb0cbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4524a05ac17de1be9923e9a9dc9c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dbcfd0ba7e5f79063be82c76153444e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9ca0a66c298c31fec04cbfc30d7b98c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ab8b542ad8bdfa536d2314963d9701&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31736155d9fcbf91049d0a9e73805dc</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Nothing Support Team">
  <data key="d0">Nothing Support Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Nothing Support Team is the support department for the Nothing organization, providing assistance for app-related issues.&lt;SEP&gt;The Nothing Support Team provides assistance with technical issues related to Nothing Phone devices, including battery sharing, app cloning, and screen problems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06e37afdf610d89a09df8901349a725e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b51e206cee412c86265f35f8120e9d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Customer Support">
  <data key="d0">Customer Support</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Customer Support is a service provided by a company, specifically Nothing, to assist users with a wide range of technical and operational issues related to their devices, including phones, accessories, and charging problems. It encompasses support for device settings, recovery processes, account issues, product troubleshooting, and network connectivity. The service is available through various channels, such as local service centers or contact methods, and is organized as a dedicated department or team within the company. It is designed to offer users assistance with technical issues, phone functionality, and device compatibility, including specific concerns like overheating and slow charging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-36249177cb5d5f7c720a6f64a0edc813&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f522fc3ced3c136bbb28b287f215d20c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79d8dc4ced2f49b73dd01d066a09896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcacac32b6b6cffea40cb0a17d301d61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f0e791bf9a53157a462f57f05674eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06e37afdf610d89a09df8901349a725e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2af070275f346cb3aabc6679c7791a2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e598990cce04e756caad38b82dbe3eca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8238a048f616eaf02f92d0455ae0f39b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9168201d4eac75ddffe0059a4394bb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="CMF Watch">
  <data key="d0">CMF Watch</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">CMF Watch is a mobile application used to connect, pair, and manage the Watch Pro and Watch Pro 2 devices, offering a range of functionalities such as firmware updates, system settings, device settings, watch face management, custom exercise addition, and resetting the device to factory settings. It also enables users to sync data, customize settings, and manage features like contacts and health monitoring. The application may experience issues with auto-starting and connectivity, which may require troubleshooting steps. In addition to being an app, CMF Watch is also an organization that provides smartwatch accessories and services, including charging docks and health reminders, and is compatible with various devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-76cdae3356bcf4004a71c8e11a80f300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1937bef2f48d7dfa41b98235ae13df22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d88ccae3cdc762688c1e8d90c4e68c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-852b3a0efad903b6a432ebd5e7a404af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-118d2f64ec32e517a13b31894b48b9ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06e37afdf610d89a09df8901349a725e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-128e66067604ae44825d98ba3ed45122&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea57d11556bf408a29dc7c7e37398cc2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Android">
  <data key="d0">Android</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Android is a mobile operating system developed by Google, widely used on smartphones and tablets, and known for supporting various audio codecs and features such as LDAC and Google Fast Pair. It provides the platform for essential services like Find My Phone and other device management features. The Nothing X app is compatible with Android and supports the management of features on the Nothing Ear and Buds Pro earbuds, including functionality such as Fast Pair. Additionally, Android is used as a source device for transferring data to the Nothing Phone, and it is relevant for app functionality and troubleshooting. The Buds, including the CMF Buds 2 and Buds Pro, are compatible with Android operating systems starting from version 5.1 and above. Android is also integral to the setup process of switching devices to the Nothing Phone, as it is transferred to the device during the configuration. In summary, Android serves as a key operating system platform that enables compatibility, functionality, and integration with various devices and services within the Nothing ecosystem.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56220d4c1145af0000fc9cb728dc6db7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9fb365d0322c82fb6ff52dc4a7925f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8464f2a22c355940190a72202a4bd5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d866982ab2e7ced6661f8a940789dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6165e1e8378c1118b98626013d6262b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06e37afdf610d89a09df8901349a725e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d629090523155bf0dd12f9021e8a28a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c9aac607d8ab10d1f5ae9d51556e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abefe8b5c23aeae06eaa603651797d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4e6bb17059b6ce78b33dddb496db9d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27081652ef7a553b2a6096008ef80269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6dc70b538423eed2a153e23decae4c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="App Battery Usage">
  <data key="d0">App Battery Usage</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">App Battery Usage is a category of phone settings that manages how apps consume battery power.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06e37afdf610d89a09df8901349a725e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Network">
  <data key="d0">Network</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Network is a system category related to connectivity, affecting app performance and requiring checks for stability or configuration changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Network refers to the connection method used by the phone, including WiFi and mobile data, which is important for app functionality and synchronization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2af070275f346cb3aabc6679c7791a2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06e37afdf610d89a09df8901349a725e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Settings">
  <data key="d0">Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Settings is a central user interface category found on various mobile devices, including smartphones and the Nothing Phone, as well as on the Watch Pro and earbuds, allowing users to customize and configure a wide range of device functions and preferences. It provides access to essential configuration options such as network settings, including WiFi, Bluetooth, data usage, and network type; location services; security settings, such as app permissions and account integration; display settings, including brightness, always-on display, and font adjustments; and system preferences like date and time, storage management, and system updates. Additionally, Settings on the Nothing Phone includes specialized features such as Battery Share, App Clone, Android Auto, NFC configuration, and Find My Device, enabling users to manage device-specific functionalities like app pinning, call settings, and game mode. On the Watch Pro, the Settings menu allows users to adjust features such as always-on display, brightness, time, and language, as well as Bluetooth connections and sensor performance. The Settings menu also encompasses broader operational controls, such as battery usage, charging preferences, notification settings, and developer options, making it a critical interface for personalizing and managing the phone’s behavior and user experience. Overall, Settings serves as a comprehensive management interface for configuring both device hardware and software functionalities across different platforms and operating systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a79d8dc4ced2f49b73dd01d066a09896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dbf1c133d4ea12599adde2c8babfb03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01cde718609da4920ebfa164616b8d87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d52fb5275de8c3b54cbe38e612348505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65f13477800edffaf85ef49b0eb80982&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a20228c525a0011e08b219ab5989855a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9168201d4eac75ddffe0059a4394bb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27081652ef7a553b2a6096008ef80269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b8eb92f55e1f3c041c691be7b6dbda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7e41b65ef7bcc80c8f1decc9bf2928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43c5f3a3b39a02f332e40eef921a1f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-258395120725348800696992422fd798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d82ee9e80b9a4011cc5dfdad909fc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fec2c3e80ab69404ff0b23b014c07483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff9ab0e6b0a19cc3df9b2e42e60f607f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d866982ab2e7ced6661f8a940789dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d089d6dd16ac59cfa0d577b293a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2af070275f346cb3aabc6679c7791a2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-124df9689f92596c4fbc5e0e680893f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d629090523155bf0dd12f9021e8a28a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-281d19d9c4f252fd5c844c3d467ca398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8238a048f616eaf02f92d0455ae0f39b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36249177cb5d5f7c720a6f64a0edc813&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3de9a6eca983da6478af176236f5152b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce2dd4dcddbe486368b957aabc2e335&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe8e5cdde2af69f64b8ce3b5c683676&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3060d71588cf955b2b239dbba0bd791d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cd614c63bd30923f007ff94a3e7a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34426e6693364728fe244fbfe87a0629&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c73879f5f4d2c0285aa18473f689789&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abefe8b5c23aeae06eaa603651797d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6f1bc17eaf113f533442b214ae6b6dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b51e206cee412c86265f35f8120e9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea57d11556bf408a29dc7c7e37398cc2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
