</node>
<node id="App info">
  <data key="d0">App info</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">App info is a category of mobile device functions that allow users to manage individual app settings and permissions.&lt;SEP&gt;App info is a section in the App details menu where users can manage individual app settings, such as uninstallation and data usage control.&lt;SEP&gt;App info is a section within settings that allows users to view and manage permissions and data storage for individual applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d089d6dd16ac59cfa0d577b293a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36249177cb5d5f7c720a6f64a0edc813</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Permissions">
  <data key="d0">Permissions</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Permissions is a section within App info where users can grant or deny access to device features like location, microphone, etc.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Location">
  <data key="d0">Location</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">"Location is a feature on the Watch Pro and smartphones that allows the device to access geographical information through GPS or other systems."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Location is a permission category that allows apps to access the user's geographic position.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fec2c3e80ab69404ff0b23b014c07483</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Google Play Store">
  <data key="d0">Google Play Store</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Google Play Store is a digital distribution platform for Android applications and games, serving as a central marketplace where users can download, update, and manage mobile applications. It provides access to a vast library of applications and services, making it a key resource for Android users. The platform is specifically mentioned as a source for downloading and installing apps on the Nothing Phone, including the Nothing X app and ChatGPT. Similar to the iOS App Store, the Google Play Store enables users to transfer data and apps to the Nothing Phone, ensuring a seamless experience for app management on Android devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aecf49d9e86fc2b3fbfb0f065b82e03e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea3750d302ca3a5f45590d544e79cdaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbdc3aa884ec77acb84402d00879691d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-124df9689f92596c4fbc5e0e680893f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d82ee9e80b9a4011cc5dfdad909fc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="iOS App Store">
  <data key="d0">iOS App Store</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">The iOS App Store is the official application store for Apple iOS devices, used for downloading and managing applications, including the Nothing X app. It serves as a digital distribution platform where users can download, install, and update iOS applications, such as the Nothing X app, which is essential for managing Nothing Ear devices. The iOS App Store provides a centralized location for iPhone users to access a wide range of apps, including the Nothing X app, ensuring they can easily obtain and maintain the latest version of the application on their Apple devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea3750d302ca3a5f45590d544e79cdaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbdc3aa884ec77acb84402d00879691d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e908dc520371478d52528beaf43780b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-716596cbb2a7e8b3702d6ceb7f52724e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Nothing X app">
  <data key="d0">Nothing X app</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Nothing X app is a comprehensive companion application developed by Nothing, designed to manage and customize the features of various Nothing earbuds and devices. It provides users with the ability to access and configure settings such as EQ, gesture controls, and sound profiles, enhancing the audio experience of products like the Ear (open), Ear (a), Ear (stick), and CMF Buds Pro 2. Additionally, the app allows for firmware updates, ensuring that the earbuds remain up-to-date with the latest features and improvements. It also enables users to manage Bluetooth connections, dual connectivity, and Smart Dial functionality. 

The Nothing X app is not limited to earbuds alone; it serves as a tool for managing device settings, including ANC, volume control, and charging functionalities for the Neckband Pro. Furthermore, it connects to smartwatches to receive message notifications from the phone's status bar. The app is available on both Google Play and the iOS App Store, offering functionality for Ear (1) and other related products. Users can also unlock additional features and customizations through the Nothing X app, such as bass settings and enhanced audio-related features like LHDC and LDAC. In summary, the Nothing X app is a multifunctional software tool that supports a wide range of Nothing products, providing control over both hardware and software aspects to improve user experience and device performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-310bcdfd35de1b898e48e8659f40d35e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79d8dc4ced2f49b73dd01d066a09896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01cde718609da4920ebfa164616b8d87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c10ba86f3c652add8c1d23db1a9625b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27081652ef7a553b2a6096008ef80269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dbac70984f20a7113387507b57809f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ea28975423f6227a8330d76c202878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8464f2a22c355940190a72202a4bd5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242b40fbdd789fce17cd5d53222cb91d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443862ed6a46e95ac18dbc4e38f2090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e7514c9c486c31232321ac43b9689ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c9aac607d8ab10d1f5ae9d51556e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f522fc3ced3c136bbb28b287f215d20c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e908dc520371478d52528beaf43780b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4524a05ac17de1be9923e9a9dc9c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56220d4c1145af0000fc9cb728dc6db7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea3750d302ca3a5f45590d544e79cdaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-136bde614c09969c0d7fb82cc253fd47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb83fc961a06d6a2e205ffa27cd9700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1bc8f3ce2d2c5d835ffeade41737ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a93494f099711f42904d9b1378c73449&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Nothing Ear (open)">
  <data key="d0">Nothing Ear (open)</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">Nothing Ear (open) is a pair of wireless earbuds that can experience battery drainage issues due to certain settings and usage scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Nothing Ear (open) is a wireless earbud product developed by Nothing, offering features like gesture controls, Dual Connection, and varying battery life.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbdc3aa884ec77acb84402d00879691d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="CMF Buds 2">
  <data key="d0">CMF Buds 2</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">CMF Buds 2 is a model of wireless earbuds where users may need to adjust Bluetooth audio settings for optimal battery performance.&lt;SEP&gt;CMF Buds 2 is a product line of Nothing, featuring advanced audio technologies and customizable settings for improved user experience.&lt;SEP&gt;CMF Buds 2 is a product line of earbuds produced by Nothing, featuring various features such as ANC, Spatial Audio Effect, and Smart Dial functionality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="AAC">
  <data key="d0">AAC</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">AAC (Advanced Audio Codec) is a high-quality audio compression format that is widely supported across various devices for audio transmission and playback. It is supported by Ear (open), Nothing Ear, CMF Buds 2, as well as the Buds and the Neckband Pro, enabling users to experience high-quality audio through Bluetooth connections. However, AAC can affect battery consumption when used for media playback due to its higher quality encoding, which may require more processing power compared to other codecs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56220d4c1145af0000fc9cb728dc6db7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443862ed6a46e95ac18dbc4e38f2090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Developer options">
  <data key="d0">Developer options</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">"Developer options is a hidden settings menu accessible through the Settings app on Android devices, used for advanced configuration and debugging."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Developer options is a hidden set of settings on Android devices that allows users to modify advanced system parameters and settings for apps and Bluetooth.&lt;SEP&gt;Developer options is a set of advanced settings in a phone's operating system that allow users to adjust Bluetooth audio codec settings and other technical configurations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fec2c3e80ab69404ff0b23b014c07483</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Bluetooth settings">
  <data key="d0">Bluetooth settings</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Bluetooth settings allow users to configure the connection and audio codecs for Bluetooth-enabled devices such as earbuds.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Firmware update">
  <data key="d0">Firmware update</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Firmware update is a software upgrade for devices which can resolve performance or functionality issues.</data>
