  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Factory reset">
  <data key="d0">Factory reset</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Factory reset is a process that restores the phone to its original state, deleting all user data, apps, and settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Factory reset is a process that returns a device to its original state, deleting all user data and settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce2dd4dcddbe486368b957aabc2e335</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Battery drainage">
  <data key="d0">Battery drainage</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Battery drainage refers to the rapid depletion of a device's battery life, which can be caused by various factors including usage scenarios and settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Active Noise Cancellation (ANC)">
  <data key="d0">Active Noise Cancellation (ANC)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Active Noise Cancellation (ANC) is a feature in earbuds that reduces ambient noise, which may affect power consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Noise Cancellation (ANC) is a feature of CMF Buds 2 that reduces background noise up to 48dB.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Noise Cancellation (ANC) is a feature of the earbuds that reduces ambient noise to improve audio clarity. It is a key functionality discussed in the document.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Noise Cancellation (ANC) is a feature on the Ear (1) earbuds that reduces ambient noise, and it can be adjusted through the Nothing X app.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1e7514c9c486c31232321ac43b9689ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea57d11556bf408a29dc7c7e37398cc2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Transparency Mode">
  <data key="d0">Transparency Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Transparency Mode is a feature available on several earbud models, including CMF Buds, CMF Buds Pro 2, and Nothing Ear, as well as the Ear (a) device. It allows users to hear ambient sounds through the earbuds while still listening to audio playback, functioning in conjunction with or as an alternative to ANC (Active Noise Cancellation) features. This mode is useful for maintaining environmental awareness in noisy settings, such as when walking outdoors or commuting. It may also impact battery life and power consumption due to the additional processing required to filter and transmit ambient sounds. The feature is commonly described as a setting or mode that enables users to stay aware of their surroundings without fully disconnecting from the audio experience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56220d4c1145af0000fc9cb728dc6db7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ea28975423f6227a8330d76c202878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-310bcdfd35de1b898e48e8659f40d35e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e908dc520371478d52528beaf43780b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb83fc961a06d6a2e205ffa27cd9700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c10ba86f3c652add8c1d23db1a9625b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebeef135007ca56eca4d845a2c04e9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="AAC mode">
  <data key="d0">AAC mode</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">AAC mode is an audio streaming codec that is recommended to improve battery life when using Nothing earphones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Firmware Update">
  <data key="d0">Firmware Update</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Firmware Update is a process of installing new software on a device to improve performance, fix bugs, and add new features.&lt;SEP&gt;Firmware Update is a process within the Nothing X App that updates the software of earphones to enhance performance and fix issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Firmware Update is an update to the device's low-level software, accessible through the Settings menu.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea3750d302ca3a5f45590d544e79cdaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c73879f5f4d2c0285aa18473f689789</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Factory Reset">
  <data key="d0">Factory Reset</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Factory Reset is a system-level process used to restore devices to their original factory settings, which can be helpful for resolving software-related issues. It can be initiated on the Neckband Pro by long-pressing the charging case button for 10 seconds. For the Watch Pro, the Factory Reset process clears all data from the device and restarts it, and it can be accessed through the Settings menu or function list, requiring the CMF Watch app for full functionality. On the Nothing Phone, a Factory Reset clears all user data and requires prior backup and account verification to prevent data loss. Additionally, Factory Reset is used for the Ear (open) earbuds as a troubleshooting step when connectivity issues persist, and it also resets the earphones to their original factory settings when functionality or connectivity problems occur.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-76cdae3356bcf4004a71c8e11a80f300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea3750d302ca3a5f45590d544e79cdaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dbf1c133d4ea12599adde2c8babfb03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39d4901014b867cda8bfaf59458315b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Battery Life">
  <data key="d0">Battery Life</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Battery Life is a critical performance attribute across various devices, including the Buds Pro earbuds, Watch Pro series, Nothing Ear (open), Ear (2), Ear (1), and the Neckband Pro. For the Buds Pro earbuds, Battery Life encompasses both earbud and case usage, with actual duration varying based on usage conditions. Similarly, the Watch Pro series exhibits different Battery Life metrics depending on usage modes and conditions. The Nothing Ear (open) has specified Battery Life durations for continuous music and communication, influenced by usage, settings, and environmental factors. 

The Ear (2) provides varying Battery Life durations depending on usage scenarios such as music playback, calls, and ANC settings. The Neckband Pro's Battery Life is contingent on the mode of operation and whether ANC or Transparency Mode is enabled. Both Ear (1) and Ear (a) earbuds, along with their charging cases, have Battery Life that depends on ANC settings, communication modes, and charging methods, such as wired charging. 

Additionally, Battery Life in the context of a phone refers to the duration it can operate on a single charge, which is affected by factors like usage patterns, temperature, and charging habits. Tips for extending phone Battery Life include proper charging practices and adjustments in settings. Overall, Battery Life is a dynamic metric that is influenced by the device type, usage conditions, features enabled, and environmental factors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d88ccae3cdc762688c1e8d90c4e68c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbeb4732200e7559b14badeb7c65f47c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbdc3aa884ec77acb84402d00879691d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-258395120725348800696992422fd798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb83fc961a06d6a2e205ffa27cd9700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1bc8f3ce2d2c5d835ffeade41737ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9ca0a66c298c31fec04cbfc30d7b98c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-716596cbb2a7e8b3702d6ceb7f52724e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4e6bb17059b6ce78b33dddb496db9d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6dc70b538423eed2a153e23decae4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Voice Calls">
  <data key="d0">Voice Calls</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Voice Calls are a specific usage scenario that significantly impacts battery consumption of earphones, as highlighted in the document.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Environmental Interference">
  <data key="d0">Environmental Interference</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Environmental Interference refers to external factors that can disrupt Bluetooth signal strength, affecting the battery life and performance of earphones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Charging Case">
  <data key="d0">Charging Case</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Charging Case is a physical component and accessory used to charge and store earbuds, primarily associated with Nothing Ear products. It serves as a housing unit that contains the earbuds and provides additional battery life when used in conjunction with them. The Charging Case includes an LED indicator for battery status, a charging port, and pogo pins that facilitate the charging connection. It may also need to be reset to resolve pairing issues or initiate reconnections, and some versions feature a Smart Dial for control functions. In certain cases, the Charging Case can play a role in performing a factory reset. It is compatible with power cables for charging and may support wireless charging, depending on the model. Additionally, the Charging Case is used for charging CMF Earbuds and Ear (1) earbuds, and its functionality is contingent upon proper maintenance, such as keeping the charging port clean and ensuring compatibility with the charging protocol.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea3750d302ca3a5f45590d544e79cdaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbdc3aa884ec77acb84402d00879691d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de2595701f68717f24b26c16e73fef62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443862ed6a46e95ac18dbc4e38f2090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efdc5389f3967066ca146a24ea33b83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e7514c9c486c31232321ac43b9689ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca8764057d5d820c4c3fb502a440d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1bc8f3ce2d2c5d835ffeade41737ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39d4901014b867cda8bfaf59458315b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e598990cce04e756caad38b82dbe3eca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Phone">
  <data key="d0">Phone</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The phone is a general term for a mobile device, which includes both iPhone and Android models, and serves as a central computing device used for making calls, running online meeting applications, and managing a variety of features and settings such as location services, WiFi Hotspot, app pinning, battery management, and data usage. It is the device used by individuals to interact with through its lock screen, camera, and other functionalities, and is integral to the operation of connected accessories like Nothing Ear products, including the Ear (1) earbuds and Ear (open) earbuds. The phone allows for Bluetooth connectivity, enabling features such as call ringing, app synchronization, and managing the settings of the earbuds. It is also used to connect with and manage devices like a smartwatch or the Watch Pro, sending notifications and facilitating communication. Additionally, the phone is involved in various operations, including enabling Battery Saver, activating Find My Device, and transferring data. It may experience technical issues such as power consumption, charging problems, and audio malfunctions, requiring troubleshooting steps to maintain its functionality. The phone's compatibility with Bluetooth devices, such as CMF Earbuds, can sometimes pose challenges, and it plays a key role in the overall ecosystem of connected devices, particularly those manufactured by Nothing Phone.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-748aef9e02744a06105085d3fb0c0fd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9168201d4eac75ddffe0059a4394bb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe8e5cdde2af69f64b8ce3b5c683676&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-258395120725348800696992422fd798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7729ae6048c026d1b7b5e466d0f1c36c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d52fb5275de8c3b54cbe38e612348505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cd614c63bd30923f007ff94a3e7a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e7514c9c486c31232321ac43b9689ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d629090523155bf0dd12f9021e8a28a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a93494f099711f42904d9b1378c73449&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39d4901014b867cda8bfaf59458315b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abefe8b5c23aeae06eaa603651797d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8238a048f616eaf02f92d0455ae0f39b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4e6bb17059b6ce78b33dddb496db9d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea57d11556bf408a29dc7c7e37398cc2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Nothing Customer Service">
  <data key="d0">Nothing Customer Service</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Nothing Customer Service is a support service provided by Nothing, designed to assist users with questions or issues related to their products and services. It serves as the support channel for resolving technical problems associated with Nothing earbuds, including features such as ANC (Active Noise Cancellation), volume control, and location functionality. As the support division of the company, it is responsible for addressing both technical and customer-related inquiries, offering troubleshooting steps and assistance for device-related issues. The service is specifically tailored to users of Nothing Ear and related products, ensuring they receive reliable support for their devices' features and overall usage experience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea3750d302ca3a5f45590d544e79cdaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e908dc520371478d52528beaf43780b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efdc5389f3967066ca146a24ea33b83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dbcfd0ba7e5f79063be82c76153444e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e7514c9c486c31232321ac43b9689ae</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Nothing OS">
  <data key="d0">Nothing OS</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Nothing OS is the operating system used by Nothing devices, including smartphones and earbuds such as the Nothing Phone and Ear (2) earbuds. It is based on Android, specifically Android 14, and offers a customizable platform for managing device settings and features. Nothing OS provides users with the ability to manually check for and install software updates, ensuring the device remains up-to-date. It also supports advanced functionalities like firmware updates, gesture control for earbuds, EQ adjustments, and integration with features such as Find My Phone and Bluetooth tethering. Version 1.1.4 and higher of Nothing OS are noted for integrating device customizations, including those for Ear (open) and Ear (2) earbuds, allowing users to access and manage earbud-related settings within the Device Details section. Additionally, Nothing OS includes a unique Glyph Interface and supports the integration of Ear (1) and Ear (stick) for seamless feature access. It also enables the hiding of app icons, offering a more personalized user experience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56220d4c1145af0000fc9cb728dc6db7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79d8dc4ced2f49b73dd01d066a09896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-136bde614c09969c0d7fb82cc253fd47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe8e5cdde2af69f64b8ce3b5c683676&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cecbf41a5540f78302f91235b833c7dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43c5f3a3b39a02f332e40eef921a1f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efdc5389f3967066ca146a24ea33b83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1bc8f3ce2d2c5d835ffeade41737ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9ca0a66c298c31fec04cbfc30d7b98c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39d4901014b867cda8bfaf59458315b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c73879f5f4d2c0285aa18473f689789&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-716596cbb2a7e8b3702d6ceb7f52724e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9ceda8e99b5757b3aaecad74209f71d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-748aef9e02744a06105085d3fb0c0fd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9025d462a4f9ed5f5840d5850b11449</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Ear (2)">
  <data key="d0">Ear (2)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Ear (2) is a product that supports Dual Connection and various customization features through the Nothing X app, including gesture controls, volume adjustment, and noise cancellation settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Ear (2) is another pair of earbuds, similar to Ear (1), that may experience similar functionality problems and is compared in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Ear (2) refers to a product line of earbuds, featuring various specifications and functionalities such as battery capacity, dual connection support, and noise cancellation.&lt;SEP&gt;Ear (2) refers to another product model with similar features to Ear (1), such as Bluetooth connectivity, ANC modes, and press control gestures.&lt;SEP&gt;Ear (2) refers to one of the earbuds that may have issues connecting to a device or being detected via Bluetooth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56220d4c1145af0000fc9cb728dc6db7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efdc5389f3967066ca146a24ea33b83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e7514c9c486c31232321ac43b9689ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-716596cbb2a7e8b3702d6ceb7f52724e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Ear (a)">
  <data key="d0">Ear (a)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Ear (a) is a pair of wireless earbuds with features such as noise cancellation, dual connection, battery life information, and water/dust resistance, manufactured by Nothing.&lt;SEP&gt;Ear (a) is a product line of Nothing, featuring wireless earbuds with advanced audio and control functionalities.&lt;SEP&gt;Ear (a) is a set of wireless earbuds with features like Environmental Noise Cancellation (ENC), Bluetooth connectivity, and support for various audio codecs such as LHDC and LDAC. It is compatible with Android and iOS devices and can be controlled via the Nothing X app.&lt;SEP&gt;Ear (a) is another earbud that may not automatically connect or reconnect to a device, potentially requiring troubleshooting steps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e908dc520371478d52528beaf43780b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c9aac607d8ab10d1f5ae9d51556e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efdc5389f3967066ca146a24ea33b83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbeb4732200e7559b14badeb7c65f47c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Watch Pro">
  <data key="d0">Watch Pro</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Watch Pro is a line of smartwatch devices manufactured by Nothing, offering a range of functionalities such as time setting, music control, heart rate monitoring, sleep tracking, stress measurement, and weather forecasting. It supports various health and activity metrics, including step count, distance, speed, blood oxygen levels, and sleep data, utilizing technologies like the Gsensor algorithm and GPS. The device connects to the CMF Watch app, enabling users to customize settings, receive notifications, monitor health metrics, and adjust features such as screen brightness and volume. While it provides Bluetooth connectivity for music control and call management, it does not support direct Bluetooth headphone connection or NFC/eSIM services. The Watch Pro is also dust and water resistant with a specific battery capacity, and its battery life varies depending on the usage mode. It requires proper wear and firmware updates to ensure accurate health tracking and correct synchronization with the CMF Watch app. Additionally, it may experience issues such as Bluetooth pairing problems with a phone, time synchronization errors, and difficulties with weather updates, which can be resolved through troubleshooting steps outlined in the related documentation. The Watch Pro supports multiple operating systems and languages, and includes a removable strap for customization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-76cdae3356bcf4004a71c8e11a80f300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fec2c3e80ab69404ff0b23b014c07483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1937bef2f48d7dfa41b98235ae13df22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d88ccae3cdc762688c1e8d90c4e68c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1887c3e753e5f27cc1105a32465893f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f73d28d893bcd51ecb5c4b3b1f54870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-852b3a0efad903b6a432ebd5e7a404af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf93869f27e0db181fc1e8abda02b165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2813ffd84d05996e288b7ae91da38439&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dbac70984f20a7113387507b57809f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c923c17927fa4e291cc287467061e0cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efdc5389f3967066ca146a24ea33b83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-118d2f64ec32e517a13b31894b48b9ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fde4d61094019d5f75532f5f5f817f6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a20228c525a0011e08b219ab5989855a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6dc70b538423eed2a153e23decae4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31736155d9fcbf91049d0a9e73805dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea57d11556bf408a29dc7c7e37398cc2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Device">
  <data key="d0">Device</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Device is a general term referring to any electronic device, such as smartphones or wearables, that may experience Bluetooth connectivity problems with earbuds or other devices.&lt;SEP&gt;The device refers to the electronic equipment being charged by the adaptor, which can experience overheating or slow charging if not used under optimal conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e598990cce04e756caad38b82dbe3eca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efdc5389f3967066ca146a24ea33b83a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Ear (open)">
  <data key="d0">Ear (open)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Ear (open) is a product line of wireless Bluetooth earbuds offered by Nothing, designed to connect to various devices including Android and iOS smartphones. These earbuds feature environmental noise cancellation and support gesture-based control functions when paired with a phone, allowing users to manage playback, call handling, and other features through simple hand movements. However, they do not include active noise cancellation (ANC) support. The product comes with a charging case that has specific charging and status indicators, and the earbuds themselves are rated for water and dust resistance at IP54. Additionally, Ear (open) is associated with sound performance and user settings, and users are recommended to utilize the Nothing X App for sound customization. There are also mentions of potential Bluetooth connection issues, which are similar to those reported with the CMF earbuds, suggesting that Ear (open) may be a product name referring to the same or a closely related model, possibly with a typo or alternative naming convention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a1887c3e753e5f27cc1105a32465893f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7729ae6048c026d1b7b5e466d0f1c36c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443862ed6a46e95ac18dbc4e38f2090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4524a05ac17de1be9923e9a9dc9c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dbcfd0ba7e5f79063be82c76153444e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39d4901014b867cda8bfaf59458315b9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="CMF Buds Pro 2">
  <data key="d0">CMF Buds Pro 2</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">CMF Buds Pro 2 are a specific model of earbuds that are discussed in the context of reconnection behavior and device compatibility.&lt;SEP&gt;CMF Buds Pro 2 is a model of earbuds produced by Nothing, featuring active noise cancellation and customizable sound settings.&lt;SEP&gt;CMF Buds Pro 2 is a pair of wireless earphones with various features, including spatial audio, battery life specifications, and call handling capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The CMF Buds Pro 2 is a line of wireless earbuds with advanced features such as noise cancellation, customized EQ settings, and support for various audio formats and pairing technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The CMF Buds Pro 2 is a wireless earbud product that uses touch controls and can be connected to multiple devices simultaneously, featuring LDAC audio encoding and noise cancellation modes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-310bcdfd35de1b898e48e8659f40d35e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242b40fbdd789fce17cd5d53222cb91d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dbcfd0ba7e5f79063be82c76153444e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39d4901014b867cda8bfaf59458315b9</data>
