</node>
<node id="CMF Earbuds">
  <data key="d0">CMF Earbuds</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">CMF Earbuds are wireless audio devices used for phone calls and online meetings, and may have compatibility issues with certain platforms or devices.&lt;SEP&gt;CMF Earbuds are wireless earbuds that support dual connection via Bluetooth and have gesture control features for managing audio playback and calls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7729ae6048c026d1b7b5e466d0f1c36c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca8764057d5d820c4c3fb502a440d2f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Gesture Control">
  <data key="d0">Gesture Control</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Gesture Control is a feature in Ear (stick) that enables users to control audio functions through touch-based commands, managed via the Nothing X app.&lt;SEP&gt;Gesture Control is a feature of Ear (2) that allows users to control audio playback and other functions through hand gestures, though it is not supported by default and requires app customization.&lt;SEP&gt;Gesture Control is a feature of the earbuds that allows users to control music playback and volume, but may not function properly due to app compatibility or incorrect touch areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Gesture Control refers to the set of control functions on the Neckband Pro, such as long-press, press, double press, and triple press, which allow users to interact with the device through physical gestures.&lt;SEP&gt;Gesture Control refers to the touch-based methods used to control the functions of the Buds, such as double-tap, triple-tap, and tap-and-hold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbad053247bfe41ce192c651034259c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-136bde614c09969c0d7fb82cc253fd47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7729ae6048c026d1b7b5e466d0f1c36c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-716596cbb2a7e8b3702d6ceb7f52724e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebeef135007ca56eca4d845a2c04e9d0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Volume Control">
  <data key="d0">Volume Control</data>
  <data key="d1">technology</data>
  <data key="d2">Volume Control is a function of the earbuds that may not work due to Bluetooth protocol compatibility issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7729ae6048c026d1b7b5e466d0f1c36c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Nothing X">
  <data key="d0">Nothing X</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Nothing X is a company or organization that develops earbuds and provides a mobile app for controlling its products.&lt;SEP&gt;Nothing X is a mobile application developed by Nothing, allowing users to customize and manage various features of Ear (a) including ANC settings, dual connection, and battery status indicators.&lt;SEP&gt;Nothing X is an application developed by Nothing, a technology company, used for configuring and managing features of the Neckband Pro, such as equalizer settings, ANC, and Ultra Bass Technology.&lt;SEP&gt;The Nothing X is an application used to manage earbuds and firmware updates, specifically mentioned for resolving Bluetooth compatibility issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2ea28975423f6227a8330d76c202878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea57d11556bf408a29dc7c7e37398cc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbeb4732200e7559b14badeb7c65f47c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="CMF earbuds">
  <data key="d0">CMF earbuds</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">CMF earbuds are a line of wireless earbuds with various control features including gesture controls, noise cancellation modes, and volume adjustment.&lt;SEP&gt;CMF earbuds are a product line of earbuds that require proper charging and maintenance to function correctly.&lt;SEP&gt;CMF earbuds are another product or brand mentioned in the context of sound quality, with similar recommendations for sound customization using the Nothing X App.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54f0e791bf9a53157a462f57f05674eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ea28975423f6227a8330d76c202878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1887c3e753e5f27cc1105a32465893f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
