<node id="Active Noise Cancellation">
  <data key="d0">Active Noise Cancellation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Active Noise Cancellation is a feature found in several earbud models, including the CMF earbuds, Ear (a), Nothing Ear, Buds Pro, Buds, and CMF Buds Pro 2. This technology is designed to reduce ambient noise, thereby enhancing the audio listening experience by providing clearer sound during playback. On the Ear (a) model, Active Noise Cancellation operates in real-time and includes an adjustable mode called Smart ANC, which adapts to varying environmental noise levels. Additionally, Ear (2) supports up to 40db of noise cancellation. The feature is particularly beneficial during calls, as it helps minimize unwanted background noise. Across all these devices, Active Noise Cancellation plays a key role in improving the overall audio quality and user experience by effectively filtering out external disturbances.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56220d4c1145af0000fc9cb728dc6db7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ea28975423f6227a8330d76c202878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbeb4732200e7559b14badeb7c65f47c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e908dc520371478d52528beaf43780b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c10ba86f3c652add8c1d23db1a9625b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebeef135007ca56eca4d845a2c04e9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Dual Connection">
  <data key="d0">Dual Connection</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Dual Connection is a feature available across several Nothing earbud models, including Ear (2), CMF Buds 2, CMF Buds Pro 2, and the Neckband Pro, allowing them to connect to two Bluetooth devices simultaneously. This functionality enables the earbuds to switch audio playback between devices based on connection priority and activity, with the primary device determined by which one is actively in use, such as for calls or audio playback. The feature is managed through the Nothing X app, which provides users with the ability to switch between connected devices and configure settings related to audio source priority and gesture controls. 

While Dual Connection is generally described as enabling simultaneous connection to two devices, some descriptions note that the Nothing X app can only control one device at a time, suggesting a limitation in device management. Additionally, there are mentions that Dual Connection may lead to potential compatibility issues or sound output delays in certain scenarios, though these are not universally reported. Overall, the feature enhances user convenience by allowing seamless transitions between devices, with specific rules governing how audio sources are prioritized and managed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ea28975423f6227a8330d76c202878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbeb4732200e7559b14badeb7c65f47c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbdc3aa884ec77acb84402d00879691d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1887c3e753e5f27cc1105a32465893f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e908dc520371478d52528beaf43780b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca8764057d5d820c4c3fb502a440d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-716596cbb2a7e8b3702d6ceb7f52724e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c10ba86f3c652add8c1d23db1a9625b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Gesture Controls">
  <data key="d0">Gesture Controls</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Gesture Controls are a feature of the Nothing Ear (open) that allows users to interact with the device through physical gestures, such as pressing the side of the earbud.&lt;SEP&gt;Gesture Controls are control methods on CMF earbuds that use tapping and holding to execute commands like volume control and noise cancellation mode switching.&lt;SEP&gt;Gesture Controls are interaction methods that allow users to control audio playback and call functions through touch actions on CMF earbuds.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2ea28975423f6227a8330d76c202878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca8764057d5d820c4c3fb502a440d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbdc3aa884ec77acb84402d00879691d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="LDAC">
  <data key="d0">LDAC</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">LDAC (Advanced Audio Coding) is a high-resolution audio codec that supports streaming rates of 990kbps, enabling less compressed audio files and better sound fidelity.&lt;SEP&gt;LDAC is a high-definition audio codec that enables high-quality audio streaming between a compatible device and earphones, supporting 24-bit depth, 96kHz sampling rate, and 990kbps bitrate.&lt;SEP&gt;LDAC is a high-definition audio codec that provides high-quality audio streaming, with support for higher bit rates, sample rates, and bit depths compared to standard codecs.&lt;SEP&gt;LDAC is a high-quality audio encoding format that supports higher bitrates and better sound quality, commonly used with Bluetooth audio devices.&lt;SEP&gt;LDAC is an audio codec supported by Nothing Ear for high-resolution audio playback.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242b40fbdd789fce17cd5d53222cb91d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca8764057d5d820c4c3fb502a440d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c9aac607d8ab10d1f5ae9d51556e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Call">
  <data key="d0">Call</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A Call is a communication session initiated between two or more devices, which affects the behavior of CMF earbuds in terms of audio output and control prioritization.&lt;SEP&gt;Call is a category of activity that can be managed using touch gestures on the Buds Pro earbuds, including answering, hanging up, or rejecting calls.&lt;SEP&gt;Call is a function of the Buds that allows users to manage incoming and outgoing calls via touch gestures, including answering, hanging up, and rejecting calls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebeef135007ca56eca4d845a2c04e9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca8764057d5d820c4c3fb502a440d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Audio Output">
  <data key="d0">Audio Output</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Audio Output refers to the process by which CMF earbuds send sound to the connected device, depending on the active device or call state.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ca8764057d5d820c4c3fb502a440d2f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Nothing Tech">
  <data key="d0">Nothing Tech</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Nothing Tech is the company that produces the Nothing X app and CMF earbuds, providing user support and product instructions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ca8764057d5d820c4c3fb502a440d2f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Google Play">
  <data key="d0">Google Play</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">Google Play is a digital distribution platform where the Nothing X App can be downloaded for Android users.&lt;SEP&gt;Google Play is a platform for downloading mobile applications, specifically used for Android users to access the Nothing X app.&lt;SEP&gt;Google Play is a platform where the Nothing X App can be downloaded for Android users.&lt;SEP&gt;Google Play is a platform where the Nothing X app can be downloaded for Android users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e908dc520371478d52528beaf43780b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca8764057d5d820c4c3fb502a440d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-716596cbb2a7e8b3702d6ceb7f52724e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="QR Code">
  <data key="d0">QR Code</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">QR Code is a type of matrix barcode used to direct users to download the Nothing X app from the official website.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ca8764057d5d820c4c3fb502a440d2f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="LDAC high-definition audio encoding">
  <data key="d0">LDAC high-definition audio encoding</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">LDAC high-definition audio encoding is a proprietary audio codec used for high-quality audio transmission over Bluetooth, which is supported by Nothing X app for optimal playback performance.&lt;SEP&gt;LDAC high-definition audio encoding is a type of audio compression technology used for high-quality sound playback over Bluetooth, supported by certain Android devices but not iOS.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c10ba86f3c652add8c1d23db1a9625b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Touch Controls">
  <data key="d0">Touch Controls</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Touch Controls are the physical and software-based controls on the CMF Buds Pro 2 used to navigate functions, such as skipping tracks or adjusting noise cancellation modes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="iOS">
  <data key="d0">iOS</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">iOS is a mobile operating system developed by Apple, primarily for iPhones and iPads, and it is compatible with various devices, including the Nothing Ear, Watch Pro, and Buds Pro earbuds. It allows users to connect their devices and use features such as audio playback and device management through compatible applications like the Nothing X app and other associated software. iOS supports Bluetooth connectivity for these products, but it has limited support for high-quality audio codecs, only supporting AAC. It does not support LDAC or LHDC codecs over Bluetooth. Additionally, iOS is mentioned as a compatibility platform for the CMF Buds 2 and the Buds, which can function with devices running iOS 13 and above.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8464f2a22c355940190a72202a4bd5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c9aac607d8ab10d1f5ae9d51556e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27081652ef7a553b2a6096008ef80269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6dc70b538423eed2a153e23decae4c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Reconnection">
  <data key="d0">Reconnection</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Reconnection refers to the process where the CMF Buds Pro 2 attempts to reconnect to previously paired devices when they come back into range, following specific priority rules.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Connection Priority">
  <data key="d0">Connection Priority</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Connection Priority is the set of rules that determine which device the CMF Buds Pro 2 connects to when multiple devices are in range, depending on their activity state.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Music State">
  <data key="d0">Music State</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Music State refers to the condition where a device is actively playing audio through the CMF Buds Pro 2, influencing connection behavior and reconnection rules.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Call State">
  <data key="d0">Call State</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Call State refers to when a device is in an active call, which affects the reconnection behavior of the CMF Buds Pro 2 as it disables connection switching.&lt;SEP&gt;Call State refers to when the Neckband Pro is handling an incoming or outgoing call from a connected device, which can prevent certain connection switches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbad053247bfe41ce192c651034259c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Head-Related Transfer Function (HRTF)">
  <data key="d0">Head-Related Transfer Function (HRTF)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Head-Related Transfer Function (HRTF) is a model used by the Spatial Audio Effect feature to simulate a 3D audio experience for users of the Neckband Pro.&lt;SEP&gt;Head-Related Transfer Function (HRTF) is a model used in creating spatial audio effects, which simulate the way sound arrives at the ears from different directions.&lt;SEP&gt;Head-Related Transfer Function (HRTF) is a model used to create spatial audio effects, enhancing the 3D sound experience.&lt;SEP&gt;Head-Related Transfer Function (HRTF) is an audio modeling technique used in the Spatial Audio Effect to simulate directional sound for an immersive experience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-310bcdfd35de1b898e48e8659f40d35e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Spatial Audio Effect">
  <data key="d0">Spatial Audio Effect</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Spatial Audio Effect is a feature of CMF Buds Pro 2 that creates a 3D audio experience with immersive sound.&lt;SEP&gt;Spatial Audio Effect is a feature of the Neckband Pro that creates a 3D immersive sound experience using HRTF models, allowing users to enjoy cinema-grade audio without limitations on audio sources.&lt;SEP&gt;Spatial Audio Effect is a feature that uses the Head-Related Transfer Function (HRTF) model to create an immersive audio experience with directional sound.&lt;SEP&gt;Spatial Audio Effect is a technology built on HRTF model, providing cinematic-grade 3D spatial sound for an immersive listening experience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-310bcdfd35de1b898e48e8659f40d35e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="ANC">
  <data key="d0">ANC</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">ANC, which stands for Active Noise Cancellation, is a noise reduction technology that utilizes microphones to detect ambient noise and generate inverse sound waves to cancel it out. This feature is present in several earbuds and headphones, including the CMF Buds Pro 2, the Buds, the Nothing Ear, and the Neckband Pro. The CMF Buds Pro 2 supports ANC and hybrid noise cancellation up to 45 dB, while the CMF Buds 2 features ANC with a maximum cancellation of 48 dB. The Neckband Pro includes ANC with up to 50 dB noise cancellation and also offers environmental adaptive ANC, which adjusts noise cancellation based on surroundings. Additionally, the Neckband Pro's ANC feature affects battery life and audio performance. It is important to note that the Nothing Ear (open) does not support ANC, meaning it lacks noise reduction capabilities. Overall, ANC enhances listening experience by reducing background noise, providing clearer audio during both music playback and calls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8464f2a22c355940190a72202a4bd5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-310bcdfd35de1b898e48e8659f40d35e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242b40fbdd789fce17cd5d53222cb91d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbdc3aa884ec77acb84402d00879691d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb83fc961a06d6a2e205ffa27cd9700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-716596cbb2a7e8b3702d6ceb7f52724e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Call Handling">
  <data key="d0">Call Handling</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Call Handling refers to the functionality of CMF Buds Pro 2 when managing calls between two connected devices, including muting music, switching audio channels, and prioritizing control gestures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-310bcdfd35de1b898e48e8659f40d35e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Smart ANC Algorithm">
  <data key="d0">Smart ANC Algorithm</data>
  <data key="d1">technology</data>
  <data key="d2">The Smart ANC Algorithm is an automatic noise cancellation system that detects the user's wearing status and external noise levels to optimize noise reduction parameters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242b40fbdd789fce17cd5d53222cb91d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Google Fast Pair">
  <data key="d0">Google Fast Pair</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Google Fast Pair is a Bluetooth pairing feature and wireless connectivity protocol that enables quick, seamless, and secure connection between devices and various earbud models. It is supported by multiple devices, including the Ear (a), Neckband Pro, Ear (2), Buds, and CMF Buds 2, as well as the Nothing Ear. This technology allows for automatic pairing with compatible Android devices and also supports connection to iOS devices. The feature is designed to provide a more convenient and efficient way to pair earbuds with phones, enhancing user experience by reducing the manual steps typically required for Bluetooth setup.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8464f2a22c355940190a72202a4bd5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242b40fbdd789fce17cd5d53222cb91d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c9aac607d8ab10d1f5ae9d51556e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Swift Pair">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Swift Pair</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Swift Pair is a wireless pairing technology designed to enable quick and seamless connection of Bluetooth devices to compatible Windows devices. It is supported by several earbud models, including Ear (2), Ear (a), Neckband Pro, Buds, and CMF Buds 2, as well as Nothing Ear. This feature simplifies the pairing process, allowing users to connect their earbuds with ease and efficiency, enhancing the user experience by reducing the complexity typically associated with Bluetooth setup.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242b40fbdd789fce17cd5d53222cb91d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c9aac607d8ab10d1f5ae9d51556e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="IP55 Protection Rating">
  <data key="d0">IP55 Protection Rating</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The IP55 Protection Rating is a standard that indicates the level of dust and water resistance of the earphones, providing protection against dust and limited water exposure under controlled conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242b40fbdd789fce17cd5d53222cb91d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Smart Dial">
  <data key="d0">Smart Dial</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">Smart Dial is a feature of the CMF Buds 2 that allows users to customize functions through rotating, clicking, and holding actions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Smart Dial is a control feature on the Neckband Pro used to adjust volume, switch between noise cancellation modes, and perform other functions such as pausing music or answering calls.&lt;SEP&gt;The Smart Dial is a control feature on the charging case of the earbuds that allows for noise cancellation mode changes and can be temporarily disabled through specific app settings.&lt;SEP&gt;The Smart Dial is a customizable feature of the charging case that allows users to control functions such as volume and noise cancellation mode through physical interactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbad053247bfe41ce192c651034259c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e7514c9c486c31232321ac43b9689ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-242b40fbdd789fce17cd5d53222cb91d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Low Lag Mode">
  <data key="d0">Low Lag Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Low Lag Mode is a feature within the CMF Buds 2 that reduces latency in audio transmission, allowing for more responsive sound synchronization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Ultra Bass Technology">
  <data key="d0">Ultra Bass Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultra Bass Technology is a feature of the Buds Pro that enhances low-frequency sounds in real time, making bass more powerful and dynamic.&lt;SEP&gt;Ultra Bass Technology is a feature of the CMF Buds 2 series that enhances low-frequency audio performance in real time, with customization options via the Nothing X app.&lt;SEP&gt;Ultra Bass Technology is a feature of the Neckband Pro that dynamically enhances low-frequency audio signals for a more powerful and personalized bass experience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Adaptive Mode">
  <data key="d0">Adaptive Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Adaptive Mode is a noise control feature that adjusts noise cancellation based on the surrounding environment to optimize audio listening experience.&lt;SEP&gt;Adaptive Mode is a setting in Ear (2) that adjusts noise cancellation in real-time based on ambient noise levels to provide optimal listening experience.&lt;SEP&gt;Adaptive Mode is a type of noise control in Ear (a) that adjusts noise cancellation based on the environment. It is part of the broader Active Noise Cancellation category and is enabled through specific user actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Adaptive Mode is an audio setting in Nothing Ear that allows the device to automatically adjust noise cancellation based on environmental noise levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbeb4732200e7559b14badeb7c65f47c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="LE Audio">
  <data key="d0">LE Audio</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">"LE Audio is a Bluetooth audio standard that Ear (open) does not support, indicating a limitation in its wireless audio capabilities."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;LE Audio is a Bluetooth audio standard that Ear (2) does not support, which may impact audio streaming capabilities on certain devices.&lt;SEP&gt;LE Audio is a Bluetooth audio standard that Nothing Ear does not support.&lt;SEP&gt;LE Audio is a Bluetooth audio standard that the Neckband Pro does not support, indicating a limitation in its connectivity capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;LE Audio is a Bluetooth audio standard, and the CMF Buds 2 does not support it as indicated in the text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443862ed6a46e95ac18dbc4e38f2090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Dirac Opteo">
  <data key="d0">Dirac Opteo</data>
  <data key="d1">technology</data>
  <data key="d2">Dirac Opteo is a digital sound enhancement technology used in CMF Buds 2 to optimise audio quality with patented correction methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Dirac Opteo is a sound enhancement technology that digitally optimizes audio performance by correcting sound colorations and maximizing acoustic quality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8464f2a22c355940190a72202a4bd5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c</data>
