  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Buds">
  <data key="d0">Buds</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Buds refers to the earbuds product line, which includes features like voice assistant, gesture control, noise cancellation, and dual connectivity.&lt;SEP&gt;The Buds are wireless earphones with various features such as battery life, ANC, and sound enhancement technology. They are part of the Nothing product line and are described in terms of their specifications and capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebeef135007ca56eca4d845a2c04e9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8464f2a22c355940190a72202a4bd5a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Voice Assistant">
  <data key="d0">Voice Assistant</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Voice Assistant is a feature available across several Nothing devices, including the Watch Pro 2, Buds Pro, Buds, Neckband Pro, and Nothing Ear (open). On the Watch Pro 2, it functions as a built-in everyday tool that allows users to interact with the device through voice commands. Similarly, the Voice Assistant on the Buds Pro and Buds can be activated via specific touch gestures, enabling users to use voice commands for device control and enhancing convenience. The Neckband Pro also includes Voice Assistant, which can be activated through the Nothing X app using specific gestures. Additionally, the Nothing Ear (open) features a Voice Assistant that can be activated through specific gestures, allowing users to interact with an AI-powered assistant. Overall, Voice Assistant is a built-in feature across these devices, designed to improve user convenience by enabling voice-activated commands and interactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dbdc3aa884ec77acb84402d00879691d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebeef135007ca56eca4d845a2c04e9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2666978485c7758b69e3c834ba80fefe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-128e66067604ae44825d98ba3ed45122</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Dual Connectivity">
  <data key="d0">Dual Connectivity</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Dual Connectivity is a feature allowing the Buds to connect to two devices simultaneously, with specific rules for disconnection and reconnection.&lt;SEP&gt;Dual Connectivity is a feature of the Neckband Pro allowing it to connect to two devices simultaneously and switch sound output based on the active device's state.&lt;SEP&gt;Dual Connectivity is a feature that allows the Buds Pro earbuds to connect to two devices simultaneously. This requires the Nothing X app to be installed and configured.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebeef135007ca56eca4d845a2c04e9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbad053247bfe41ce192c651034259c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb83fc961a06d6a2e205ffa27cd9700</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Music/Standby">
  <data key="d0">Music/Standby</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Music/Standby is a function within the Buds that allows users to control playback through gestures, such as double-tap to skip forward or triple-tap to skip back.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebeef135007ca56eca4d845a2c04e9d0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Buds Pro">
  <data key="d0">Buds Pro</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Buds Pro are wireless earbuds that support various features such as touch controls, voice assistant activation, and noise cancellation modes, and are compatible with Android and iOS devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Transparency mode">
  <data key="d0">Transparency mode</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Transparency mode is a feature of the Buds Pro that allows ambient sounds to be heard through the earbuds while still providing audio playback.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="ENC">
  <data key="d0">ENC</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">ENC stands for Environmental Noise Cancellation, a feature found in various earbuds and earphones models, including the Ear (open), Nothing Ear, Ear (stick), and Buds Pro. This feature utilizes microphones to remove background noise during calls, thereby ensuring clearer communication and preventing others from hearing the user's surroundings. As a specific type of noise cancellation, ENC is part of the ANC (Active Noise Cancellation) feature set, and it is designed to optimize microphone performance to enhance call clarity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f443862ed6a46e95ac18dbc4e38f2090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb83fc961a06d6a2e205ffa27cd9700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c9aac607d8ab10d1f5ae9d51556e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27081652ef7a553b2a6096008ef80269</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Touch area">
  <data key="d0">Touch area</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The touch area is a sensitive part of the Buds Pro earbuds used to trigger gestures and functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8</data>
