<node id="Music Mode">
  <data key="d0">Music Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Music Mode is a category of usage mode for the Buds Pro earbuds, where audio playback occurs with specific battery life and ANC settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ecb83fc961a06d6a2e205ffa27cd9700</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Call Mode">
  <data key="d0">Call Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Call Mode is a category of usage mode for the Buds Pro earbuds, where the earbuds are used for voice communication with specific battery life and ANC settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ecb83fc961a06d6a2e205ffa27cd9700</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="ANC mode">
  <data key="d0">ANC mode</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">ANC mode is a category of operational setting that modifies battery life and noise cancellation performance in the Buds Pro earbuds.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ecb83fc961a06d6a2e205ffa27cd9700</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Wireless Charging">
  <data key="d0">Wireless Charging</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Wireless charging is a method of charging a phone or device without using a cable, and it is supported by certain devices. Specifically, the Nothing Phone supports wireless charging at 15W Qi standard and also offers 5W reverse charging for other devices. It can be charged using a wireless charger compatible with Qi and 9V1.6A standards, taking approximately 110 minutes to charge from 0 to 100%. Additionally, the Nothing Ear earbuds support wireless charging, allowing users to charge the device without a wired connection. However, it is important to note that not all devices support this feature; for instance, the Phone (2a) Plus does not support wireless charging, and the Nothing Ear (open) also does not support it, relying on wired charging methods instead. Similarly, the Buds Pro earbuds and the Neckband Pro do not support wireless charging, requiring users to charge them via a Type-C cable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbdc3aa884ec77acb84402d00879691d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dbf1c133d4ea12599adde2c8babfb03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb83fc961a06d6a2e205ffa27cd9700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-281d19d9c4f252fd5c844c3d467ca398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcde7317fc7b036415d89ea81329b232&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9025d462a4f9ed5f5840d5850b11449</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Fast Charging">
  <data key="d0">Fast Charging</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Fast charging is a feature available across several devices, including the Nothing Phone, Nothing Ear (open), Nothing Ear, and the Neckband Pro. It allows for rapid battery replenishment, significantly reducing charging time while providing extended usage time. On the Nothing Phone, fast charging is enabled using PD3.0/QC4.0 technology, offering a maximum power output of 33W. The Nothing Ear (open) and Nothing Ear earbuds are capable of delivering up to 2.6 hours of ANC OFF playback after just 10 minutes of charging. Similarly, the Neckband Pro provides 18 hours of continuous music playback with a 10-minute charge, although this may vary depending on the use of ANC and other modes. The Phone (2a) Plus also supports fast charging, with specific recommendations for optimal use. Overall, fast charging serves as a convenient feature for quick battery top-ups, enhancing user experience by minimizing downtime.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbdc3aa884ec77acb84402d00879691d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dbf1c133d4ea12599adde2c8babfb03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb83fc961a06d6a2e205ffa27cd9700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-716596cbb2a7e8b3702d6ceb7f52724e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcde7317fc7b036415d89ea81329b232</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Ultra Bass">
  <data key="d0">Ultra Bass</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultra Bass is a sound enhancement technology in the Buds that dynamically adjusts bass levels in real time based on the user's listening preferences.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8464f2a22c355940190a72202a4bd5a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="IP54">
  <data key="d0">IP54</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">"IP54 is a rating under IEC standard 60529 for water and dust resistance, indicating that Ear (open) can withstand limited water exposure and dust ingress."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;IP54 is a rating for water and dust resistance of the Nothing Ear earbuds, under IEC standard 60529, indicating protection against dust and water jets.&lt;SEP&gt;IP54 is a rating indicating the level of dust and water resistance for the Buds, as defined by the IEC 60529 testing standard.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8464f2a22c355940190a72202a4bd5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443862ed6a46e95ac18dbc4e38f2090</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Neckband Pro">
  <data key="d0">Neckband Pro</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Neckband Pro is a product line by Nothing, featuring wireless earphones with various functionalities such as battery life, waterproofing, and dual connectivity.&lt;SEP&gt;The Neckband Pro is a product model from CMF by Nothing, featuring various audio and connectivity functionalities such as battery life and microphone performance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Neckband Pro is a wireless earphone device that supports dual connectivity and offers various control functions, including volume adjustment, noise cancellation mode switching, and call handling.&lt;SEP&gt;The Neckband Pro is a wireless earphone product that offers various features including ANC, Ultra Bass, Spatial Audio Effect, and support for Bluetooth technologies and pairing options.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbad053247bfe41ce192c651034259c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="CMF">
  <data key="d0">CMF</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">CMF is the brand name associated with the Neckband Pro, collaborating with Dirac for audio tuning and providing support for the product's features.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Dirac">
  <data key="d0">Dirac</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Dirac is a company that collaborates with CMF by Nothing to provide audio tuning and customizable sound effects for the Neckband Pro.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Equalizer Settings">
  <data key="d0">Equalizer Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Equalizer Settings refer to the customizable audio preferences available on the Neckband Pro through the Nothing X app, including predefined sound effects and user settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Connection Snatch">
  <data key="d0">Connection Snatch</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Connection Snatch is an event where the Neckband Pro switches connection from one device to another, based on the current state of devices and user interaction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbad053247bfe41ce192c651034259c3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
