<node id="Music Playback">
  <data key="d0">Music Playback</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Music Playback refers to the state when the Neckband Pro is playing audio from a connected device, which can trigger changes in device connections or sound output.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbad053247bfe41ce192c651034259c3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Reset Function">
  <data key="d0">Reset Function</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Reset Function is a category of operations on the Neckband Pro that allows users to reset the device by holding the Smart Dial and function button for 5 seconds.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbad053247bfe41ce192c651034259c3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Volume Adjustment">
  <data key="d0">Volume Adjustment</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Volume Adjustment is a category of functions available on the Neckband Pro, allowing users to increase or decrease the audio volume using the Smart Dial.&lt;SEP&gt;Volume Adjustment is a feature of Ear (2) that can be customized through the Nothing X app, though it is not supported by default gesture control.&lt;SEP&gt;Volume Adjustment is a feature of Watch Pro that allows users to modify the audio output level while exercising.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbad053247bfe41ce192c651034259c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6dc70b538423eed2a153e23decae4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-716596cbb2a7e8b3702d6ceb7f52724e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Noise Cancellation Mode">
  <data key="d0">Noise Cancellation Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Noise Cancellation Mode is a category of settings on the Neckband Pro, enabling users to switch between Active Noise Cancellation and Transparency Mode for audio experience customization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbad053247bfe41ce192c651034259c3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Bluetooth 5.3">
  <data key="d0">Bluetooth 5.3</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">"Bluetooth 5.3 is a wireless communication standard that enables the Ear (open) to connect with compatible devices, offering improved performance and connectivity features."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Bluetooth 5.3 is a wireless communication protocol version that the Ear (a) earbuds use for connectivity, offering improved performance and features compared to earlier versions.&lt;SEP&gt;Bluetooth 5.3 is the version of Bluetooth technology used by the Neckband Pro for wireless connectivity and communication with compatible devices.&lt;SEP&gt;Bluetooth 5.3 is the wireless communication protocol used by Nothing Ear for connectivity with devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443862ed6a46e95ac18dbc4e38f2090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c9aac607d8ab10d1f5ae9d51556e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Equalizer presets">
  <data key="d0">Equalizer presets</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Equalizer presets are customizable audio profiles available on the Neckband Pro, including Balanced, More Bass, More Treble, and Voice, which can be adjusted via the Nothing X app.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="IP55 rating">
  <data key="d0">IP55 rating</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The IP55 rating indicates the Neckband Pro's resistance to dust and water, but it is not designed for water sports or use during showers, and its protective performance may degrade over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Headphones">
  <data key="d0">Headphones</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">Headphones refer to the Neckband Pro earphones, which are part of the product and have features such as ANC, Ultra Bass, and Spatial Audio Effect, with specific power-off behavior after 120 minutes of inactivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="IEC 60529">
  <data key="d0">IEC 60529</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">IEC 60529 is an international standard for the degree of protection provided by enclosures of electrical equipment, used to define the waterproof capabilities of the Neckband Pro.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Hotspot">
  <data key="d0">Hotspot</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Hotspot is a feature on the Nothing Phone that allows WiFi sharing, but it can cause high energy consumption and heat issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Hotspot is a feature that allows the phone to create a WiFi network, enabling other devices to connect and access the internet through the phone's data connection.&lt;SEP&gt;Hotspot is a feature that allows the phone to share its internet connection wirelessly, but it results in increased power consumption and heat generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Hotspot is a feature that allows users to share their phone’s internet connection with other devices, though it may cause increased energy consumption and heat.&lt;SEP&gt;Hotspot is a feature that enables the phone to share its internet connection via WiFi, which may cause increased battery consumption and heat.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cecbf41a5540f78302f91235b833c7dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27081652ef7a553b2a6096008ef80269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-748aef9e02744a06105085d3fb0c0fd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43c5f3a3b39a02f332e40eef921a1f87</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="App pinning">
  <data key="d0">App pinning</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">App pinning is a feature on the Nothing Phone that allows users to keep an app open and visible while using other apps, potentially increasing security risks.&lt;SEP&gt;App pinning is a security feature allowing users to keep an app in view and enable it to access personal data or open other apps, managed through the device settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3de9a6eca983da6478af176236f5152b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Screen casting">
  <data key="d0">Screen casting</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Screen casting is the process of mirroring or displaying the phone's screen on a TV or other device within the same local area network.&lt;SEP&gt;Screen casting is the process of mirroring the screen of a device to a TV or other display, accessible through quick settings on the device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3de9a6eca983da6478af176236f5152b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="IEC 629">
  <data key="d0">IEC 629</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">IEC 60529 is an international standard that defines the degree of protection provided by enclosures of electrical equipment, specifically used to classify the waterproofing capabilities of the Neckband Pro.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Battery Capacity">
  <data key="d0">Battery Capacity</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Battery capacity refers to the power storage capability of various devices. The Phone (2a) Plus has a battery capacity of 5000 mAh, providing extended usage without frequent recharging. The Ear (2) earbuds have a battery capacity of 33 mAh for the earbuds themselves, while their charging case offers 485 mAh. Phone 1 is equipped with a battery capacity of 5000 mAh. The Nothing Phone also features a battery capacity of 5000 mAh, ensuring long-lasting performance. In contrast, the Neckband Pro has a lower battery capacity of 220 mAh, which influences its overall usage time and performance in different modes. Additionally, the total power storage of the Phone (2) is 4700 mAh.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bd5bdbf50fdf619063eece8e9e67241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9ff89b42c8123f60ebe4521bfb0cbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-281d19d9c4f252fd5c844c3d467ca398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcde7317fc7b036415d89ea81329b232</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="App Pinning">
  <data key="d0">App Pinning</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">App Pinning is a feature that allows users to keep specific apps visible on the home screen, with potential risks to privacy and security when apps are pinned.&lt;SEP&gt;App Pinning is a feature that keeps an app in view on the device, with potential privacy and security implications.&lt;SEP&gt;App Pinning is a phone feature that keeps an app visible on the screen, with potential privacy implications if it accesses personal data.&lt;SEP&gt;App Pinning is a security feature that keeps an app in view and potentially enables access to personal data or interaction with other apps, managed through device settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffe8e5cdde2af69f64b8ce3b5c683676&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-748aef9e02744a06105085d3fb0c0fd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d52fb5275de8c3b54cbe38e612348505</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Screen Casting">
  <data key="d0">Screen Casting</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Screen Casting is a feature that allows users to mirror their phone's display to a TV or other device, typically requiring both devices to be on the same local area network. This functionality is accessible via quick settings and involves the transmission of screen content to a target device such as a television. The Nothing Phone supports Screen Casting through WiFi Direct connections, which enable seamless screen sharing. All descriptions consistently highlight the core purpose of Screen Casting as a screen mirroring process, with the method of connectivity being either WiFi Direct or a shared local area network, depending on the device and implementation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffe8e5cdde2af69f64b8ce3b5c683676&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-258395120725348800696992422fd798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d52fb5275de8c3b54cbe38e612348505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3060d71588cf955b2b239dbba0bd791d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-748aef9e02744a06105085d3fb0c0fd0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Repair Status">
  <data key="d0">Repair Status</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Repair Status refers to the process of tracking the progress of a repair request for a device, which is done through a specific online link.&lt;SEP&gt;Repair Status refers to the tracking of a device's repair progress, available only to users who applied for repair online.&lt;SEP&gt;Repair Status refers to the tracking of device repairs, typically done through an online link provided by Nothing for users who applied for repair services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-748aef9e02744a06105085d3fb0c0fd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff9ab0e6b0a19cc3df9b2e42e60f607f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Photos App">
  <data key="d0">Photos App</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Photos app is a built-in application on the phone that allows users to manage and view photos and videos, including those in the deleted bin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="System Update">
  <data key="d0">System Update</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A System Update is a software update process for the Nothing Phone that involves installing the latest version of the Nothing OS. It is released periodically to improve performance, fix issues, and add new features. The System Update feature allows users to upgrade the phone's software via WiFi, ensuring that the latest bug fixes and enhancements are applied. This update process is typically initiated through the Settings menu, where users can access and apply the update to maintain optimal device functionality. As a category of software maintenance, System Update serves to resolve bugs or improve features by providing the latest operating system version to the device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-258395120725348800696992422fd798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7b5b1eb951ce536bdbb599b623332a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcde7317fc7b036415d89ea81329b232&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bd5bdbf50fdf619063eece8e9e67241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9ff89b42c8123f60ebe4521bfb0cbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0028e301a1da668320afc0e2e78601b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27081652ef7a553b2a6096008ef80269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b51e206cee412c86265f35f8120e9d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Guest User">
  <data key="d0">Guest User</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Guest User is an account type that allows secure sharing of the device without access to personal data, recommended when using app pinning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Google">
  <data key="d0">Google</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Google is a multinational technology company that provides a wide range of services and features, including account management, app downloads, backup, cloud storage, and device tracking. It offers services such as Find My Device, which allows users to locate and secure their devices, and Google Photos, used for backup and data management on the Nothing Phone. Google's services are integrated into the Nothing Phone's features, enabling functionalities like account verification, data recovery, and software updates. Additionally, Google provides location-based services, lock screen settings, and app management options through its Find My Phone service. The company also supports backup processes for the Nothing Phone when connected to WiFi and left on standby for 2 hours to charge. Overall, Google plays a central role in enhancing user experience through its ecosystem of services and features on smartphones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a9fb365d0322c82fb6ff52dc4a7925f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3de9a6eca983da6478af176236f5152b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dbf1c133d4ea12599adde2c8babfb03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe8e5cdde2af69f64b8ce3b5c683676&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d866982ab2e7ced6661f8a940789dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb46e252d3a2a9cb08cfababdb615773&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d52fb5275de8c3b54cbe38e612348505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-124df9689f92596c4fbc5e0e680893f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d82ee9e80b9a4011cc5dfdad909fc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c73879f5f4d2c0285aa18473f689789&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b8eb92f55e1f3c041c691be7b6dbda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-748aef9e02744a06105085d3fb0c0fd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43c5f3a3b39a02f332e40eef921a1f87</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Find My Phone">
  <data key="d0">Find My Phone</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Find My Phone is a service provided by Google that allows users to locate, lock, or erase their lost or stolen device using a Google account and internet connectivity. It is a location-based feature that enables users to find their phone's approximate location and trigger a ring if the device is turned on and connected to a network. This functionality is available through the Google website and can also be accessed via the Watch Pro 2, which includes Find My Phone as a built-in tool to help users locate their phone, thereby enhancing device security. To use the feature, the phone must be on and with network access enabled, and users need to be signed in with their Google account. In addition to locating the device, Find My Phone provides the ability to send notifications, enable locks, and secure account information if the phone is lost or stolen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a9fb365d0322c82fb6ff52dc4a7925f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e55e3fed26fabdb52106695b9582ce3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cecbf41a5540f78302f91235b833c7dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe8e5cdde2af69f64b8ce3b5c683676&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d866982ab2e7ced6661f8a940789dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41ebb68d062de192afe8e06b1a67a1c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0028e301a1da668320afc0e2e78601b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c73879f5f4d2c0285aa18473f689789&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-281d19d9c4f252fd5c844c3d467ca398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34426e6693364728fe244fbfe87a0629&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2666978485c7758b69e3c834ba80fefe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-128e66067604ae44825d98ba3ed45122&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-748aef9e02744a06105085d3fb0c0fd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9025d462a4f9ed5f5840d5850b11449</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Screen Recording">
  <data key="d0">Screen Recording</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Screen Recording is a feature used for screen casting, accessible through quick settings on the device.&lt;SEP&gt;Screen Recording is a mobile device functionality used to capture video of the phone's screen, accessible through quick settings and settings menus on the Nothing Phone.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a9fb365d0322c82fb6ff52dc4a7925f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c73879f5f4d2c0285aa18473f689789</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Lock Screen">
  <data key="d0">Lock Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Lock Screen is a feature of a mobile device that provides security and access control to the phone's interface. It is the interface that appears when the device is locked, allowing users to manage screen lock options such as password, PIN, or pattern. Additionally, the Lock Screen can be configured for privacy settings, including the visibility of message details and the ability to hide messages. It also features options to manage notifications and preview them without unlocking the device. On the Nothing Phone, the Lock Screen refers to a security feature that requires a password or PIN to access and is used for account verification during certain operations like factory reset. Overall, the Lock Screen serves as a critical component in protecting personal data and controlling device access.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9dbf1c133d4ea12599adde2c8babfb03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d089d6dd16ac59cfa0d577b293a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d52fb5275de8c3b54cbe38e612348505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cd614c63bd30923f007ff94a3e7a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c73879f5f4d2c0285aa18473f689789&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-748aef9e02744a06105085d3fb0c0fd0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Software Update">
  <data key="d0">Software Update</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Software Update is a process that allows the phone to receive new features, security patches, and system improvements via the operating system, which can be checked manually in the settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Software Update is a process that allows users to upgrade the Nothing OS to the latest version through WiFi, with instructions to avoid interrupting the update.&lt;SEP&gt;Software Update is a process that checks for and installs new versions of the operating system, which can be manually initiated or prompted by the system.&lt;SEP&gt;Software Update is a system update feature that provides new software versions to the phone, often accompanied by notifications and can be manually checked through Settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Software Update refers to the process of updating the device's operating system, with notifications sent via Nothing OS and accessible through the Settings menu.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cecbf41a5540f78302f91235b833c7dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe8e5cdde2af69f64b8ce3b5c683676&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d52fb5275de8c3b54cbe38e612348505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c73879f5f4d2c0285aa18473f689789&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-748aef9e02744a06105085d3fb0c0fd0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="USB Debugging">
  <data key="d0">USB Debugging</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">USB Debugging is a developer-oriented feature available on the Nothing Phone, as well as other Android devices, that allows for communication between the device and a PC over a USB connection. This feature enables advanced troubleshooting, command execution, file transfers, and log retrieval. It is typically accessed through the Developer Options in the System settings category, which can be enabled via the phone's Settings menu. Once activated, USB Debugging provides deeper device connectivity and control, facilitating more detailed device configurations, testing, and technical management. It is an essential tool for developers and advanced users who require enhanced functionality and diagnostic capabilities when interacting with the device through a connected computer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77d37b7781a21f9ace596c3bcb0cbfd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9fb365d0322c82fb6ff52dc4a7925f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe8e5cdde2af69f64b8ce3b5c683676&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d866982ab2e7ced6661f8a940789dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7b5b1eb951ce536bdbb599b623332a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9ff89b42c8123f60ebe4521bfb0cbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0028e301a1da668320afc0e2e78601b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c73879f5f4d2c0285aa18473f689789&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6f1bc17eaf113f533442b214ae6b6dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcde7317fc7b036415d89ea81329b232&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b51e206cee412c86265f35f8120e9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9025d462a4f9ed5f5840d5850b11449</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="App Locker">
  <data key="d0">App Locker</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">App Locker is a category of security features that enables app encryption and access control, supported by Nothing OS 2.0.0.&lt;SEP&gt;App Locker is a security feature in the Settings category of the Nothing Phone that allows users to lock specific apps for added privacy and protection.&lt;SEP&gt;App Locker is a security feature that allows users to lock specific apps to prevent unauthorized access, enhancing device security.&lt;SEP&gt;App Locker is a security feature that allows users to lock specific apps, with settings accessible through the Settings menu.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d866982ab2e7ced6661f8a940789dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b51e206cee412c86265f35f8120e9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c73879f5f4d2c0285aa18473f689789&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6f1bc17eaf113f533442b214ae6b6dd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Dark Theme">
  <data key="d0">Dark Theme</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Dark Theme is a display option that changes the phone's interface to a dark mode, configurable through the Settings menu or by swiping down on the home screen.&lt;SEP&gt;Dark Theme is a display setting that allows users to change the visual theme of the device interface, accessible through Settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Dark Theme is a display setting that changes the phone's color scheme to a darker version, improving readability in low light and offering aesthetic preferences.&lt;SEP&gt;Dark Theme is a visual setting option on the Nothing Phone, accessible through the Settings &gt; Display menu, allowing users to switch between light and dark UI modes.&lt;SEP&gt;Dark Theme is a visual setting that changes the device's interface to a dark mode, accessible via the Settings menu.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-36249177cb5d5f7c720a6f64a0edc813&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d866982ab2e7ced6661f8a940789dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34426e6693364728fe244fbfe87a0629&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c73879f5f4d2c0285aa18473f689789&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6f1bc17eaf113f533442b214ae6b6dd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Quick Settings">
  <data key="d0">Quick Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Quick Settings is a feature of a mobile device that allows users to access common functions and settings with a single swipe or tap.&lt;SEP&gt;Quick Settings is a feature on smartphones that provides easy access to various functions and settings, such as enabling Battery Saver.&lt;SEP&gt;Quick Settings is a panel accessible from the lock screen or by swiping down, allowing users to toggle device functions such as camera, airplane mode, and clock features.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8cd614c63bd30923f007ff94a3e7a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d089d6dd16ac59cfa0d577b293a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abefe8b5c23aeae06eaa603651797d38</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Camera">
  <data key="d0">Camera</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Camera is a hardware and software feature on the Nothing Phone that allows users to take photos and videos. It can be accessed from the lock screen using specific gestures, as described in the user manual and setup instructions. The Camera includes settings for controlling the recording light, managing location data, and configuring wireless connectivity options. Additionally, it is an application that enables photo and video capture with features such as location saving and GPS integration. As a category of mobile device functionality, the Camera encompasses the ability to capture and manage images and videos, and may sometimes be subject to performance issues such as slowness or freezing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea3750d302ca3a5f45590d544e79cdaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce2dd4dcddbe486368b957aabc2e335&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d866982ab2e7ced6661f8a940789dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d089d6dd16ac59cfa0d577b293a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d52fb5275de8c3b54cbe38e612348505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3060d71588cf955b2b239dbba0bd791d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cd614c63bd30923f007ff94a3e7a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65f13477800edffaf85ef49b0eb80982&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6f1bc17eaf113f533442b214ae6b6dd</data>
