<node id="Storage">
  <data key="d0">Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Storage is a category of mobile device functions that manage data space and files on the device. It refers to the internal memory space of the phone used for saving files, apps, photos, and other data, and it can be managed through settings. Specifically, Storage is a section within the Settings app that provides options for managing device storage, including clearing cache and temporary files. This section enables users to clean up space by removing temporary files and optimize storage usage. Overall, Storage on the phone refers to the capacity for saving data and files, and it requires management through settings or built-in tools to free up space.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-36249177cb5d5f7c720a6f64a0edc813&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce2dd4dcddbe486368b957aabc2e335&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d089d6dd16ac59cfa0d577b293a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cd614c63bd30923f007ff94a3e7a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8238a048f616eaf02f92d0455ae0f39b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7e41b65ef7bcc80c8f1decc9bf2928</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Device lock">
  <data key="d0">Device lock</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Device lock is a category of mobile device settings that manage screen lock options, including PIN, Pattern, and Password.&lt;SEP&gt;Device lock is a feature in the Security &amp; privacy section of the Nothing Phone that allows users to set up screen lock methods like pattern, PIN, fingerprint, and face recognition.&lt;SEP&gt;Device lock is a security setting on the Nothing Phone that allows users to choose their preferred unlocking method, such as pattern, PIN, or biometric authentication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b8eb92f55e1f3c041c691be7b6dbda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d089d6dd16ac59cfa0d577b293a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d82ee9e80b9a4011cc5dfdad909fc2</data>
