<node id="SIMs">
  <data key="d0">SIMs</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">SIMs are small chips used in mobile devices to connect to cellular networks, and their settings can be adjusted for data usage and network selection.&lt;SEP&gt;SIMs are the SIM cards in the device that allow network access and can be used to switch between 4G and 5G networks.&lt;SEP&gt;SIMs is a sub-section under Network &amp; Internet that allows users to configure settings for each SIM card, including data usage and preferred network types.&lt;SEP&gt;SIMs is a sub-section within Network &amp; internet that allows users to manage their SIM card settings and network preferences.&lt;SEP&gt;SIMs is a subcategory under Network &amp; internet that allows users to manage multiple SIM cards and their data usage settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-36249177cb5d5f7c720a6f64a0edc813&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d089d6dd16ac59cfa0d577b293a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cd614c63bd30923f007ff94a3e7a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65f13477800edffaf85ef49b0eb80982&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7e41b65ef7bcc80c8f1decc9bf2928</data>
