<node id="Airplane Mode">
  <data key="d0">Airplane Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Airplane Mode is a category of mobile device functions that disables all wireless connectivity features to prevent interference with aircraft systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Airplane Mode is a device setting that disables all wireless communication, including cellular, Wi-Fi, and Bluetooth connections.&lt;SEP&gt;Airplane Mode is a device setting that disables wireless functions such as WiFi, Bluetooth, and cellular data, enabling users to control network connectivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Airplane Mode is a feature that disables all wireless communication functions on the phone, such as WiFi, Bluetooth, and cellular data.&lt;SEP&gt;Airplane mode is a setting that disables all wireless functions on the phone, including WiFi, Bluetooth, and cellular data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcacac32b6b6cffea40cb0a17d301d61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d089d6dd16ac59cfa0d577b293a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cd614c63bd30923f007ff94a3e7a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8238a048f616eaf02f92d0455ae0f39b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7e41b65ef7bcc80c8f1decc9bf2928</data>
