<node id="MMS">
  <data key="d0">MMS</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is a feature within the SMS application that allows for sending images and videos through text messaging. It is a category of mobile communication designed to transmit multimedia messages, such as images and videos, over data networks or WiFi, as opposed to standard text SMS. To operate correctly, MMS requires proper network settings and a functioning SIM card. The service enables users to send richer content compared to traditional SMS, leveraging mobile networks to facilitate the transmission of multimedia data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ce2dd4dcddbe486368b957aabc2e335&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-258395120725348800696992422fd798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d089d6dd16ac59cfa0d577b293a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2af070275f346cb3aabc6679c7791a2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cd614c63bd30923f007ff94a3e7a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7e41b65ef7bcc80c8f1decc9bf2928</data>
