<node id="USB OTG">
  <data key="d0">USB OTG</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">USB OTG (USB On The Go) is a standard enabling mobile devices to connect directly to each other, allowing data transfer and charging from external devices like a U disk.&lt;SEP&gt;USB OTG (USB On The Go) is a standard that allows mobile devices to communicate with each other, enabling direct data transfer and charging capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;USB OTG (USB On The Go) is a standard that allows mobile devices to connect and communicate directly with other devices, such as a U disk.&lt;SEP&gt;USB OTG (USB On The Go) is a standard that allows mobile devices to connect directly to each other or external storage.&lt;SEP&gt;USB OTG (USB On The Go) is a standard that allows mobile devices to connect directly to each other, enabling data transfer and charging functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77d37b7781a21f9ace596c3bcb0cbfd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e55e3fed26fabdb52106695b9582ce3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-258395120725348800696992422fd798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7b5b1eb951ce536bdbb599b623332a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0028e301a1da668320afc0e2e78601b</data>
