</node>
<node id="Data roaming">
  <data key="d0">Data roaming</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Data roaming refers to the use of data services through a network that doesn't belong to the user's home region, such as browsing the internet, watching videos, or sending emails while abroad. It often incurs higher fees.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e55e3fed26fabdb52106695b9582ce3b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="USB debugging">
  <data key="d0">USB debugging</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">"USB debugging is a developer setting that enables a phone to communicate with a computer for development and debugging purposes."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;USB debugging is a developer mode for the phone to communicate with the PC over a USB connection, allowing for sending commands, files, and retrieving log information from the Android device.&lt;SEP&gt;USB debugging is a developer option that allows for more detailed device diagnostics and communication with computers.&lt;SEP&gt;USB debugging is a developer option that allows more detailed communication between the device and a computer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e55e3fed26fabdb52106695b9582ce3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fec2c3e80ab69404ff0b23b014c07483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34426e6693364728fe244fbfe87a0629&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36249177cb5d5f7c720a6f64a0edc813</data>
