<node id="USB Tethering">
  <data key="d0">USB Tethering</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">USB Tethering is a feature allowing the Nothing Phone to share its internet connection with a connected computer, functioning as a WiFi router when connected via USB.&lt;SEP&gt;USB Tethering is a feature that allows a phone to share its internet connection with a computer via a USB cable.&lt;SEP&gt;USB Tethering is a feature that allows a smartphone to share its internet connection with a connected PC via USB.&lt;SEP&gt;USB Tethering is a feature that allows the phone to share its internet connection with a PC via a USB cable, functioning as a WiFi router.&lt;SEP&gt;USB tethering is a feature that allows a phone to act as a WiFi router and share its internet connection with a connected PC.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77d37b7781a21f9ace596c3bcb0cbfd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-258395120725348800696992422fd798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7b5b1eb951ce536bdbb599b623332a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bd5bdbf50fdf619063eece8e9e67241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9ff89b42c8123f60ebe4521bfb0cbd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="WiFi Direct">
  <data key="d0">WiFi Direct</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">WiFi Direct is a wireless connection technology that enables devices to connect and share files directly over WiFi. It offers faster transfer speeds compared to Bluetooth and provides a greater range for short-range connections. As a networking protocol, WiFi Direct allows for secure and efficient file transfer between nearby devices, making it a key feature for nearby sharing and screen-casting. Its capabilities are particularly useful for fast transfers and screen-casting on Phone (2a).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77d37b7781a21f9ace596c3bcb0cbfd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-258395120725348800696992422fd798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7b5b1eb951ce536bdbb599b623332a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3060d71588cf955b2b239dbba0bd791d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bd5bdbf50fdf619063eece8e9e67241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9ceda8e99b5757b3aaecad74209f71d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ab8b542ad8bdfa536d2314963d9701</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="4G">
  <data key="d0">4G</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">4G is a cellular data standard that provides high-speed internet connectivity for mobile devices.&lt;SEP&gt;4G is a telecommunications standard for mobile broadband, offering faster data speeds than 3G but slower than 5G.&lt;SEP&gt;4G is a wireless communication standard that provides high-speed internet access and can be switched with 5G in certain networks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8238a048f616eaf02f92d0455ae0f39b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bd5bdbf50fdf619063eece8e9e67241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce2dd4dcddbe486368b957aabc2e335</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="WiFi 6">
  <data key="d0">WiFi 6</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">WiFi 6 is a newer generation of wireless networking technology that enhances speed and efficiency for internet connectivity.&lt;SEP&gt;WiFi 6 is a wireless networking standard supported by Phone (2a), offering faster internet speeds and improved connectivity.&lt;SEP&gt;WiFi 6 is a wireless networking standard supported by the Nothing Phone, offering improved speed and efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;WiFi 6 is a wireless networking standard that offers faster speeds and better performance compared to previous WiFi versions, and the Nothing Phone supports it.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1bd5bdbf50fdf619063eece8e9e67241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0028e301a1da668320afc0e2e78601b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3060d71588cf955b2b239dbba0bd791d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ab8b542ad8bdfa536d2314963d9701</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Dual SIM Dual Standby">
  <data key="d0">Dual SIM Dual Standby</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Dual SIM Dual Standby is a specific mode of dual SIM operation where both phone numbers are in standby but cannot perform calls or data access at the same time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1bd5bdbf50fdf619063eece8e9e67241</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="GPS">
  <data key="d0">GPS</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The GPS (Global Positioning System) is a satellite-based navigation system that enables location tracking and navigation. It is a built-in functionality on the Watch Pro 2, which activates during specific outdoor exercise modes to accurately record workout routes, track location and distance, and support movement data collection during outdoor workouts. Additionally, GPS is required for geo-tagging photos, allowing the geographical settings to be saved with them. While GPS provides accurate location tracking, it may occasionally lose signal in certain environments, potentially affecting its performance during outdoor exercises.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fec2c3e80ab69404ff0b23b014c07483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8238a048f616eaf02f92d0455ae0f39b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bd5bdbf50fdf619063eece8e9e67241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65f13477800edffaf85ef49b0eb80982&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fde4d61094019d5f75532f5f5f817f6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-128e66067604ae44825d98ba3ed45122&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31736155d9fcbf91049d0a9e73805dc</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Charging Protocol">
  <data key="d0">Charging Protocol</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Charging Protocol encompasses the methods and standards used for charging, such as PPS protocol, and how they affect charging speed and performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1bd5bdbf50fdf619063eece8e9e67241</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
