<node id="PPS Protocol">
  <data key="d0">PPS Protocol</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">"PPS protocol is a charging standard that ensures efficient and fast charging of the phone, particularly recommended for use with the Phone (2a) Plus model."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;PPS Protocol (Programmable Power Supply) is a fast charging standard that enhances charging speed and efficiency, recommended for optimal charging of Phone (2).&lt;SEP&gt;PPS Protocol is a charging standard that supports faster charging speeds when using compatible chargers like the Nothing Charger.&lt;SEP&gt;PPS Protocol is a fast charging protocol supported by Nothing Phone, enabling quicker full charging times at optimal conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1bd5bdbf50fdf619063eece8e9e67241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcde7317fc7b036415d89ea81329b232&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41ebb68d062de192afe8e06b1a67a1c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-281d19d9c4f252fd5c844c3d467ca398</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Expandable Memory">
  <data key="d0">Expandable Memory</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Expandable Memory is a feature that allows additional storage through MicroSD cards, though it is not supported by Phone 1.&lt;SEP&gt;Expandable Memory refers to the ability to add external storage to a device, which the Nothing Phone does not support.&lt;SEP&gt;Expandable Memory refers to the lack of support for external storage on the Nothing Phone, as it does not have expandable storage capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1bd5bdbf50fdf619063eece8e9e67241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0028e301a1da668320afc0e2e78601b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9025d462a4f9ed5f5840d5850b11449</data>
