<node id="Training Load">
  <data key="d0">Training Load</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Training Load is an estimate of the physical stress exerted on the body during and after a workout, based on training time, distance, and intensity, and it reflects the body's fatigue level.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2666978485c7758b69e3c834ba80fefe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Recovery Time">
  <data key="d0">Recovery Time</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Recovery Time indicates the duration required for a user to fully recover their fitness level before engaging in the next intense workout, aiding in training schedule planning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2666978485c7758b69e3c834ba80fefe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Workout Detection">
  <data key="d0">Workout Detection</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Workout Detection is a feature of the Watch Pro 2 that automatically identifies when a user is exercising and prompts them to enter the appropriate workout mode.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2666978485c7758b69e3c834ba80fefe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Aerobic Training Effect (ATE) Ratings">
  <data key="d0">Aerobic Training Effect (ATE) Ratings</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Aerobic Training Effect (ATE) Ratings classify the intensity of workouts on a scale from &lt;1.0 to 5.0, where lower ratings indicate light activity and higher ratings suggest effective or intensive training.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2666978485c7758b69e3c834ba80fefe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Anaerobic Training Effect (AnTE) Ratings">
  <data key="d0">Anaerobic Training Effect (AnTE) Ratings</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Anaerobic Training Effect (AnTE) Ratings are similar to ATE ratings but focus on anaerobic activities, classifying workout intensity from &lt;1.0 to 5.0 and indicating the physical impact on the body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2666978485c7758b69e3c834ba80fefe</data>
