<node id="Location Services">
  <data key="d0">Location Services</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Location Services are a set of technologies (GPS, GLONASS, etc.) that Watch Pro utilizes for tracking and positioning.&lt;SEP&gt;Location Services are features enabled through the Nothing Phone's integration with Google, allowing users to find their device's location using WiFi or cellular data.&lt;SEP&gt;Location Services is a feature on mobile devices that allows location tracking and is required for Find My Device to function.&lt;SEP&gt;Location Services is a feature that enables apps to access the device's location data, which is essential for services like Find My Phone to locate a device.&lt;SEP&gt;Location Services is a system feature that enables the phone to share its geolocation data, which is required for certain functions like Find My Device to work properly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9dbf1c133d4ea12599adde2c8babfb03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d866982ab2e7ced6661f8a940789dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abefe8b5c23aeae06eaa603651797d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6dc70b538423eed2a153e23decae4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-748aef9e02744a06105085d3fb0c0fd0</data>
