<node id="Always-on display (AOD)">
  <data key="d0">Always-on display (AOD)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">"Always-on display (AOD) is a feature that maintains the watch face visible on the Watch Pro screen even when not actively in use, potentially affecting brightness and battery consumption."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fec2c3e80ab69404ff0b23b014c07483</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767407143</data>
</node>
<node id="Firmware">
  <data key="d0">Firmware</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Firmware is the software embedded in electronic devices such as the Nothing Phone, Nothing Ear earbuds, Watch Pro, and Ear (stick) and Ear (1) that controls their basic functions and enables them to operate. It provides essential functionality and can be updated to resolve issues, access new features, and improve overall performance. Firmware updates for the Nothing Phone are available through the System settings category, while updates for the Nothing Ear earbuds and the Watch Pro can be performed via the Nothing X app. Additionally, firmware for Ear (stick) and Ear (1) can also be updated through the System update section in Settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-36249177cb5d5f7c720a6f64a0edc813&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fec2c3e80ab69404ff0b23b014c07483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79d8dc4ced2f49b73dd01d066a09896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-136bde614c09969c0d7fb82cc253fd47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6f1bc17eaf113f533442b214ae6b6dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9</data>
