<node id="SIM Card">
  <data key="d0">SIM Card</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A SIM card is a small chip that allows phone connectivity to a network, and can be used to switch between 4G and 5G, or to control data usage.&lt;SEP&gt;SIM Card is a hardware component used in the Nothing Phone for network connectivity, and the device supports dual SIM cards for simultaneous use.&lt;SEP&gt;SIM Card is a hardware component used in the Nothing Phone to enable cellular network connectivity, with dual SIM support mentioned for both 4G and data usage.&lt;SEP&gt;SIM Card refers to the physical card used to insert into a phone to enable network services, with Phone (2) supporting dual SIM cards.</data>
