<edge source="Nothing X App" target="Nothing Ear">
  <data key="d6">27.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The Nothing X App connects to the Nothing Ear for Bluetooth functionality, but this connection is halted during iOS calls due to system prioritization.&lt;SEP&gt;The Nothing X App is used to configure and manage various features of Nothing Ear, such as Dual Connection, Smart ANC, and Bass Enhance." &lt;| "feature management, product integration&lt;SEP&gt;The Nothing X App is used to manage and update the firmware of Nothing Ear products, showing a functional relationship between the earphone brand and its management software.</data>
  <data key="d8">9,app connectivity,app functionality,device management,device pairing</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762fda66ccc0b9dd4cae96c4b09a2422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1767407152</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Nothing X App" target="iOS Device">
  <data key="d6">17.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The Nothing X App and iOS Device have a specific interaction where Bluetooth communication is paused during calls to prioritize processing power and bandwidth.&lt;SEP&gt;The Nothing X App interacts with iOS devices through Bluetooth and is affected by their settings and protocols, particularly the BLE protocol used for low-power connections.</data>
  <data key="d8">call management,device compatibility,system prioritization</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-762fda66ccc0b9dd4cae96c4b09a2422</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1767407152</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Nothing X App" target="Android Device">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The Nothing X App on Android devices may have issues with background app management, leading to disconnections, and requires specific permissions and settings for optimal performance.</data>
  <data key="d8">background app management,system behavior</data>
