<edge source="Settings" target="Phone">
  <data key="d6">55.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The Phone is the device that users configure through the Settings menu, which is a core category of the phone that allows users to adjust various parameters that affect performance, including network type, volume levels, and data usage settings. The Settings interface serves as the main platform for configuring phone features such as Battery Share, App Pinning, Notification Management, Battery Saver, and account integration. It also provides options to manage system updates, network settings, location services, and lock screen configurations. Overall, Settings is a comprehensive category on the Phone that enables users to access and manage a wide range of functions and features to customize their device experience.</data>
  <data key="d8">configuration hub,device configuration,device control,device settings,phone management,user configuration,user control,user interaction</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-258395120725348800696992422fd798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d52fb5275de8c3b54cbe38e612348505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cd614c63bd30923f007ff94a3e7a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abefe8b5c23aeae06eaa603651797d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8238a048f616eaf02f92d0455ae0f39b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9168201d4eac75ddffe0059a4394bb79</data>
