<edge source="Google" target="Find My Phone">
  <data key="d6">45.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Find My Phone is a feature provided by Google as part of its services for device tracking and management.&lt;SEP&gt;Find My Phone is part of Google's services and is integrated into the Android ecosystem to provide device tracking and security features.&lt;SEP&gt;Find My Phone uses Google account information to locate and manage devices remotely.&lt;SEP&gt;Google provides the Find My Phone feature, which helps users locate and manage their lost devices through a Google account.&lt;SEP&gt;Google provides the Find My Phone service which is used to locate and manage lost Nothing Phone devices.</data>
  <data key="d8">account integration,device management,device security,device tracking,location tracking,remote device management,security integration,service provider,service provision</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-ffe8e5cdde2af69f64b8ce3b5c683676&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9fb365d0322c82fb6ff52dc4a7925f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d866982ab2e7ced6661f8a940789dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c73879f5f4d2c0285aa18473f689789</data>
