<edge source="Google" target="Nothing Phone">
  <data key="d6">59.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The Nothing Phone integrates various Google services to enhance its functionality and user experience. These services include Google Photos for data backup and storage of recordings, as well as Google's backup process for ensuring user data is securely preserved. Additionally, the device utilizes Google services for account management, allowing users to access their accounts and verify their identities to unlock certain features. The integration also supports app downloads, data transfer, and location tracking, demonstrating a significant reliance on Google's ecosystem. Furthermore, the Nothing Phone incorporates Google's Find My Device functionality, enabling users to locate and manage their device remotely. Overall, the partnership between Google and the Nothing Phone is evident through the seamless use of Google services for backup, synchronization, account verification, and other essential features.</data>
  <data key="d8">cloud integration,cloud services,device integration,ecosystem usage,integration,service integration,tech ecosystem,technology provider,user account</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-3a9fb365d0322c82fb6ff52dc4a7925f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3de9a6eca983da6478af176236f5152b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dbf1c133d4ea12599adde2c8babfb03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-124df9689f92596c4fbc5e0e680893f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d82ee9e80b9a4011cc5dfdad909fc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b8eb92f55e1f3c041c691be7b6dbda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43c5f3a3b39a02f332e40eef921a1f87</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1767407175</data>
</edge>
