<edge source="Nothing Phone" target="iPhone">
  <data key="d6">40.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Nothing Phone is the destination device for data transfer from iPhone as described in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;The Nothing Phone is being set up alongside an iPhone, and data is being transferred from the iPhone to the Nothing Phone as part of the switching process.&lt;SEP&gt;The transfer process involves moving data from an iPhone to a Nothing Phone, indicating a relationship between the two devices in the context of data migration.&lt;SEP&gt;iPhone is a source device for transferring data to the Nothing Phone, following a setup process that involves connecting the devices and signing in with a Google account.&lt;SEP&gt;iPhone is a source device from which data can be transferred to the Nothing Phone, indicating a transfer relationship between the two phone brands.</data>
  <data key="d8">data migration,device transfer,mobile technology,setup process,user migration</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-aecf49d9e86fc2b3fbfb0f065b82e03e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6165e1e8378c1118b98626013d6262b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d629090523155bf0dd12f9021e8a28a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abefe8b5c23aeae06eaa603651797d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4e6bb17059b6ce78b33dddb496db9d2</data>
